{
	chapter.0004F753021F792F.subtitle: "Machines that cut, press and draw metal"
	chapter.0004F753021F792F.title: "&#EAA842Machine Shop&r"
	chapter.01444FD66C887136.subtitle: "Some rocks give off more than heat."
	chapter.01444FD66C887136.title: "&#EAA842Radiation&r"
	chapter.04A46C02458195AF.subtitle: "Bodies, camps and hands"
	chapter.04A46C02458195AF.title: "&#52B788Survival&r"
	chapter.04AD47A849CCDEE3.subtitle: "Armor, packs, suits, robots and the tables that build them."
	chapter.04AD47A849CCDEE3.title: "&#E76F51Gear&r"
	chapter.0F060B9E16F27A6C.subtitle: "Brewing, experience, enchanting and Thaumaturge"
	chapter.0F060B9E16F27A6C.title: "&#EAA842Magic and Experience&r"
	chapter.0F992F6BBD0E4A5B.subtitle: "A push you can carry along a wire."
	chapter.0F992F6BBD0E4A5B.title: "&#EAA842Electricity&r"
	chapter.1F47D13EE53E4644.subtitle: "Mail to the End, and what lives in the deep dark"
	chapter.1F47D13EE53E4644.title: "&#EAA842Ender and Sculk&r"
	chapter.300E7291674AE0A7.subtitle: "Seven trees, each earned a different way."
	chapter.300E7291674AE0A7.title: "&#E76F51Skills&r"
	chapter.34FA1FFC0241A397.subtitle: "What a blow does comes from physical figures, not item names."
	chapter.34FA1FFC0241A397.title: "&#E76F51Combat&r"
	chapter.3B462A8F5EBB4A80.subtitle: "Kept books that open what you can draw and build"
	chapter.3B462A8F5EBB4A80.title: "&#EAA842Treatises&r"
	chapter.470F3AD9ED1F75BC.subtitle: "Shafts, cogs, water, and steam"
	chapter.470F3AD9ED1F75BC.title: "&#EAA842Rotation&r"
	chapter.48190EF942CBA65B.subtitle: "Six ages, entered by making something"
	chapter.48190EF942CBA65B.title: "&#EAA842Ages&r"
	chapter.4CD66899CAD50361.subtitle: "Hot ground and netherite"
	chapter.4CD66899CAD50361.title: "&#EAA842Nether&r"
	chapter.579054965C31FBE8.subtitle: "Salt, water, air and the oil under the ground"
	chapter.579054965C31FBE8.title: "&#EAA842Chemistry&r"
	chapter.6190C0260C31C601.subtitle: "A shed is not a system."
	chapter.6190C0260C31C601.title: "&#EAA842Logistics&r"
	chapter.64325D1FE0D3927F.subtitle: "Cooking, growing and keeping"
	chapter.64325D1FE0D3927F.title: "&#52B788Food&r"
	chapter.68D207779E17E0CD.subtitle: "Villages, commissions and markets"
	chapter.68D207779E17E0CD.title: "&#52B788Trading&r"
	chapter.71B9668A4E7650CB.subtitle: "Bearings, lifts, wheels, wings and the sky"
	chapter.71B9668A4E7650CB.title: "&#EAA842Vehicles and Flight&r"
	chapter.7A08CB21B8614A4B.subtitle: "A machine is never told when to stop."
	chapter.7A08CB21B8614A4B.title: "&#EAA842Control&r"
	chapter.7DC46164EF9A397B.subtitle: "Built from parts, not picked from a list."
	chapter.7DC46164EF9A397B.title: "&#E76F51Weapons&r"
	chapter.7DF200847AB5D229.subtitle: "Fire and copper through iron, steel and alloys"
	chapter.7DF200847AB5D229.title: "&#EAA842Heat&r"
	chapter_group.149BF26CB820257A.title: "&#52B788&lSurvival&r"
	chapter_group.30D13E4776495F39.title: "&#EAA842&lTechnology&r"
	chapter_group.5DFA7B32CAEFD16D.title: "&#E76F51&lCombat&r"
	quest.001F833861288838.quest_desc: ["a &6&lrelay&r lets a small current switch a large one, delegation at its finest. it has to touch an electromagnet, closes when the field is strong, and lets go when it fades. opening it under load wears it."]
	quest.001F833861288838.title: "Relay Station"
	quest.0023AC4B0A98ED49.quest_desc: ["a &6&lpropeller&r on a turning shaft pushes a craft through air. facing up it becomes a rotor. blade tips that run too fast wear out, and the reaction torque rolls the craft. the aircraft is not thrilled about this either."]
	quest.0023AC4B0A98ED49.title: "Propeller"
	quest.00B0D32E99DABB35.quest_desc: ["where a robot rests and recharges. a bed, in other words, with extra steps."]
	quest.00B0D32E99DABB35.title: "Robot Dock"
	quest.00B22E201C48801F.quest_desc: ["build a bedroll: a mattress with no frame, light enough to lash to a pack. the camper's choice." "" "the padding you choose changes how well you sleep and how much you carry."]
	quest.00B22E201C48801F.title: "Roughing It"
	quest.00E800C6BB0BD9E6.quest_desc: ["keep going until you have spent a good handful of points in the veil tree. some branches are exclusive: choosing one closes its sibling, so read before you learn. you cannot sneak back for the other one."]
	quest.00E800C6BB0BD9E6.quest_subtitle: "Spend a fair number of points."
	quest.00E800C6BB0BD9E6.title: "Veil: Spend Points"
	quest.010794AFC2A4C4CE.quest_desc: ["What a blow does comes from physical figures, not item names."]
	quest.010794AFC2A4C4CE.title: "Combat"
	quest.011C74745C519E2B.quest_desc: ["a heat source is only a heat source. make one that sustains itself, and keep it cooled." "" "&c&owarning: a reactor cannot be switched off instantly, decay heat lingers for a long time, and an overheated core builds pressure, hisses, then bursts into radioactive slag.&r you will regret this if you ignore the hissing."]
	quest.011C74745C519E2B.title: "Criticality"
	quest.016DD0AF07D0A28F.quest_desc: ["hold a &6&lcontroller&r. it is on or off only, with a limited number of cards and variables, so plan what it should decide. it is decisive, not deep."]
	quest.016DD0AF07D0A28F.title: "Get a Controller"
	quest.0191229BC9237645.quest_desc: ["the drag reader records grip: how hard the goods resist being pulled across a surface."]
	quest.0191229BC9237645.title: "Friction"
	quest.0242EAEEF85A1464.quest_desc: ["chemistry moves fluids, and pipes never pull. something has to push: a &6&lpump&r on a turning shaft, a compressor, a tray. make a pump and a &6&lvalve&r so you can start and stop a flow. a plan that relies on gravity and optimism is not a plan."]
	quest.0242EAEEF85A1464.title: "Plumbing"
	quest.02AD290CDCFA751B.quest_desc: ["a parts bin takes up to eight kinds of small pieces, none weighing over 0.2 Mu each. screws and nails by the handful, sorted for you."]
	quest.02AD290CDCFA751B.title: "Tiny Pieces"
	quest.02D3D53D1A382F6D.quest_desc: ["eight bricks in a ring. feed it fuel and it radiates heat upward. &c&owood fires are too cool for any metalwork; coal and charcoal burn hotter, and a blaze rod hotter again.&r"]
	quest.02D3D53D1A382F6D.title: "Firebox"
	quest.02D73E38016F635C.quest_desc: ["some rocks give off more than heat, and are not shy about it. find a way to hear it." "" "&c&oradiation is counted in ru.&r below a small threshold it does nothing; above it a dose builds, and sickness comes in three steps: hunger, then weakness and mining fatigue, then wither. it escalates politely, then not."]
	quest.02D73E38016F635C.title: "Something Is Ticking"
	quest.02E0F7272B435A0F.quest_desc: ["a heap of chests is storage in the way a heap of laundry is a wardrobe. a &6&lwarehouse dock&r is the end of an aisle: goods go in at any side by belt or hopper, retrieved goods come out the front, and its screen lists everything on the racks. it needs &d&o&nmechanical treatise i&r." "" "right-click it, click the title and name it. you will want to tell your docks apart."]
	quest.02E0F7272B435A0F.title: "The Dock"
	quest.0311209E1B8B1F72.quest_desc: ["use a technique from the onslaught tree. keep the rhythm, and try not to stop and admire it."]
	quest.0311209E1B8B1F72.title: "Relentless"
	quest.0342E33230F35140.quest_desc: ["a &6&lwinch&r draws a grapple line in, so a vehicle can climb or be hauled. it is the polite way to get out of a ditch."]
	quest.0342E33230F35140.title: "Winch"
	quest.037306F9170B66B4.quest_desc: ["melt copper and tin together in one crucible. mostly copper, a little tin. if the ratio is off the tank looks empty and nothing pours, so add more of the short metal. the crucible is not broken, just sulking."]
	quest.037306F9170B66B4.title: "Bronze"
	quest.03C84BB7A2AA55B0.quest_desc: ["make your first tool or part out of stainless steel, nickel, chromium, aluminum, titanium, tungsten, a carbide, cermet, netherite, osmium or their alloys. yes, that is a long list." "" "fission opens here, and space, by way of a telescope sighting of a planet. &d&o&ntreatises&r name the age their types belong to, but reading is never gated by age."]
	quest.03C84BB7A2AA55B0.title: "Alloy Age"
	quest.0474158F69CC958A.quest_desc: ["pick the worn piece under your crosshair and strike through it. armor is a set of pieces, and some pieces are softer than others, same as most of us before breakfast."]
	quest.0474158F69CC958A.title: "Soft Spot"
	quest.04B72CACE79DA952.quest_desc: ["a furnace that cannot overheat, made for tempering. needs &d&o&nmaterials treatise ii&r. the calm one in the family."]
	quest.04B72CACE79DA952.title: "Annealing Furnace"
	quest.052D43F29EA638A7.quest_desc: ["propellers are drawn at a blueprint table with this volume. light reading, one hopes."]
	quest.052D43F29EA638A7.title: "Aerospace Treatise I"
	quest.053683ADC78C7420.quest_desc: ["fresh steel is brittle or soft. heat and cooling decide which. tempering only counts while the metal cools through its band, so the timing is the whole joke."]
	quest.053683ADC78C7420.title: "Quench and Temper"
	quest.057F4A942EFF432B.quest_desc: ["wake in a bed you set down. the night was long and you won."]
	quest.057F4A942EFF432B.title: "Slept Through"
	quest.05F0FF3B164E5E8A.quest_desc: ["powder, a barrel and a steady hand (the hand is the hard part). shape the parts at a smithing table, woodworking table or stonecutter and assemble a gun at the engineering table." "" "guns are a tool type, not a list of items. see the weapons chapter for the road there."]
	quest.05F0FF3B164E5E8A.title: "Armed"
	quest.06419F0120483C04.quest_desc: ["&d&o&nelectrical treatise iii&r covers tubes, resonators, controllers and the first real circuits. this is where things start to look like a plan."]
	quest.06419F0120483C04.title: "Treatise: Circuits"
	quest.0645C3FC0A5F009A.quest_desc: ["some alloys only come right with nothing pulling the melt apart. an aluminium and lead melt in a thermal vessel standing in the gap resolves into aluminium lead. on the ground it gives nothing." "" "vessels in the gap or the end run airless, so nothing oxidises away. notice what that does to your yields."]
	quest.0645C3FC0A5F009A.title: "Casting in Free Fall"
	quest.0682BBC454BFE1E8.quest_desc: ["&c&oa heavy punch with a shockwave.&r needs &d&o&nweapons treatise i&r: blades and heads. subtle it is not."]
	quest.0682BBC454BFE1E8.title: "Knuckleblaster"
	quest.0683AE3C893A655E.quest_desc: ["a press sits directly on a shaft and brings its full weight down every stroke. it needs no linkage, because subtlety is not its thing." "" "notice that it overshoots soft metals. needs &d&o&nmechanical treatise i&r."]
	quest.0683AE3C893A655E.title: "Mechanical Press"
	quest.070E69AEE9364565.quest_desc: ["all of this is hand work, and your arm is the only power plant on site. turn it into a shaft." "" "build a hand crank from a crank arm and hold right-click to turn it. notice how little it can carry: fine for learning and for small loads, but a workshop machine will just strain and politely refuse to move."]
	quest.070E69AEE9364565.quest_subtitle: "Your arm is the first engine"
	quest.070E69AEE9364565.title: "Crank It"
	quest.07828FB75E773972.quest_desc: ["&6&laerospace treatise iii: jets&r. opens jets. subtle they are not." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with aerospace ii held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.07828FB75E773972.title: "Aerospace Treatise III"
	quest.07BB96B1E237E75F.quest_desc: ["one bonded data port and a metal plate make an &6&lendernet upgrade&r, which leashes an electric controller or computer to a data port. a leash, but for electronics."]
	quest.07BB96B1E237E75F.title: "Endernet Upgrade"
	quest.07D952AE84E61F58.quest_desc: ["Mail to the End, and what lives in the deep dark"]
	quest.07D952AE84E61F58.title: "Ender and Sculk"
	quest.0822F078A4D4E4A2.quest_desc: ["keep going until you have spent a good handful of points in the observation tree. some branches are exclusive: choosing one closes its sibling, so read before you learn. fitting advice for this tree, really."]
	quest.0822F078A4D4E4A2.quest_subtitle: "Spend a fair number of points."
	quest.0822F078A4D4E4A2.title: "Observation: Spend Points"
	quest.08429468E6B57DD3.quest_desc: ["copper over iron bends when hot, which is the most dramatic thing either metal does. place a &6&lbimetallic strip&r against a crucible and the thing you want to switch, and it trips at a set temperature." "" "notice that it overshoots. if your batch has a narrow working window, a bare strip may not be good enough."]
	quest.08429468E6B57DD3.title: "Thermostat Strip"
	quest.08653EB4288F41C0.quest_desc: ["there is also a plain way into the air. gliding works as in the base game, with zero paperwork. notice that in thin air, such as the End, a glide sinks faster: a controlled descent, not a cruise. a glide also sinks with the armor you wear, and the membrane that holds you up wears and can tear past its rating."]
	quest.08653EB4288F41C0.title: "Elytra"
	quest.08CD5BC477FFA52A.quest_desc: ["the village's notice board: open orders, contracts and notices about standing and raids. read the small print, there is a lot of it."]
	quest.08CD5BC477FFA52A.title: "Ledger Board"
	quest.096CDFF9C8FDAAF5.quest_desc: ["a &6&lsawblade&r in the tool slot of an engineering table cuts a plain block into &6&lmote&rs, the pieces of finespace. motes let you build at a fraction of block size. go on, think small."]
	quest.096CDFF9C8FDAAF5.title: "Cut It Finer"
	quest.096DC39F890D86EC.quest_desc: ["grow a crop to harvest. wheat and the mod's crops all follow the climate of the place they stand. location, location, location."]
	quest.096DC39F890D86EC.title: "Something to Eat"
	quest.098EE23DA714C964.quest_desc: ["onslaught points come from landed blows with a quick weapon, and from blows that follow close on the last one. repeats pay less, and training dummies stop paying. fast hands, slow payouts." "" "make a note once you hold some points in the onslaught tree."]
	quest.098EE23DA714C964.quest_subtitle: "Earn your first points."
	quest.098EE23DA714C964.title: "Onslaught: Earn Points"
	quest.0990178BB899BA6D.quest_desc: ["&6&lchemical treatise i: pressure vessels&r. opens pressure vessels, boilers and gas tanks, plus the mixer, vacuum pump and flare stack. a book about containing things that would rather not be contained." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level. clerics sell chemical i and ii." "" "the electrolyser also needs electrical i."]
	quest.0990178BB899BA6D.title: "Chemical Treatise I"
	quest.09CFDA00A8BCFDE1.quest_desc: ["a brick pan on top of a fire. &c&onotice how close to the flame it settles, and that a hot pan burns a bare hand.&r cosy, but rude to touch."]
	quest.09CFDA00A8BCFDE1.title: "Hearth"
	quest.0A24D5E0742A3FC6.quest_desc: ["a &6&ldata connector&r links a sensor or node to a controller. right-click the node, then the controller. long links need fine wire along the way, because distance is never free."]
	quest.0A24D5E0742A3FC6.title: "Link It Up"
	quest.0A335D31CFDA6F10.quest_desc: ["a &6&lmembrane sensor&r is a film of phantom membrane in a block. link it to a controller and it reads how sleepless the most tired player nearby is, rising to full at about an hour without sleep, plus whether anyone is in reach at all. it needs no power and only measures. &c&otwo more channels read the strongest loose toxic gas cloud nearby, and what kind it is: half for a cloud that hangs, full for a heavy one that has settled.&r"]
	quest.0A335D31CFDA6F10.title: "A Nose for Sleeplessness"
	quest.0A53E7B0B277E586.quest_desc: ["Cooking, growing and keeping"]
	quest.0A53E7B0B277E586.title: "Food"
	quest.0A5408F197C740BF.quest_desc: ["a crank needs a person. a river does not complain about overtime." "" "shape a wheel rim and place the water wheel where water actually flows past its faces. still water does nothing, however hopeful you are. it is heavy, slow to spin up and slow to stop, but it is the first source that can actually run machines."]
	quest.0A5408F197C740BF.title: "Unattended"
	quest.0A5A82A53B0BC6E6.quest_desc: ["use a reader module on a rack and it steps to the next band of that property, so the rack takes only goods recorded in that band. sneak and use it to clear. it needs no power for this, and goods with no record are refused." "" "a filtered rack that does not accept the goods is passed over even if it holds the same stack."]
	quest.0A5A82A53B0BC6E6.title: "Filtered Racks"
	quest.0A9755058F58CF8C.quest_desc: ["right-click the dock, pick a line, set an amount and press fetch. the filter sheet narrows the stock by what the heads recorded, and several bands in one row match any of them. goods stored without a head for a property are not listed when you filter on it."]
	quest.0A9755058F58CF8C.title: "Ask by Name"
	quest.0B0904C1F29F5299.quest_desc: ["the end is out of reach by hand. send something there anyway, like a very ambitious parcel. an ender port pair is made from one pearl and two plates, and moves goods when its tank holds liquid teleportant."]
	quest.0B0904C1F29F5299.title: "Mail Call"
	quest.0B1DA0DC782CF2B8.quest_desc: ["shape a &6&lhelmet&r, chestplate, leggings or boots from plate at a bench. the &6&lplate is the piece&r: it decides the armor. wear it and see, then admire yourself. any plate will do, even a shulker shell ground flat on the grinding wheel: light, tough and heat resistant." "" "slime balls can be the lining under a piece, adding armor because slime stiffens against fast blows." "" "stud plates, spaced closer for more pierce resistance and thorns at the cost of mass, and armor lining, thicker for more padding, are parts too." "" "armor you built reduces blows; see the head to toe quest in the combat chapter."]
	quest.0B1DA0DC782CF2B8.title: "Plate Is the Piece"
	quest.0B25237999E61617.quest_desc: ["&6&lmagazine&rs hold cartridges of one size for guns with a box or belt feed. the recipe decides the size, from small to drum. hold r to reload. mind the size, because the gun will not."]
	quest.0B25237999E61617.title: "Magazine"
	quest.0B30ADDA7FE01DA4.quest_desc: ["hit armor with something softer than it. it will not go well, and the weapon will be the one feeling silly." "" "damage comes from physical figures, and hardness is one of them. a soft edge on hard plate simply gives up."]
	quest.0B30ADDA7FE01DA4.title: "Wrong Tool"
	quest.0B77E3C295907BAA.quest_desc: ["eight wrought iron plates around a smithing table. heavy, expensive, and very pleased with itself."]
	quest.0B77E3C295907BAA.title: "Anvil"
	quest.0BA2ACCC7D1E0BA0.quest_desc: ["the core sits in the middle of the top face of a hollow shell of dense material, with a lattice inside. make the core itself. the shell does the heavy lifting; the core gets the glory."]
	quest.0BA2ACCC7D1E0BA0.title: "Reactor Core"
	quest.0D44C57A49029473.quest_desc: ["iron wants a hotter fire that also strips the oxygen from the ore. push more air, hold more heat, line a chamber." "" "notice that no vessel turns iron ore straight into an ingot. shortcuts were not invited."]
	quest.0D44C57A49029473.title: "Iron Needs Air"
	quest.0DE376A751A13FE2.quest_desc: ["shelves are not stasis. hot cargo cools toward room temperature and food rots, and an item is brought up to date when it is retrieved or when the stock is read about every ten seconds. set something hot on a shelf and look again later."]
	quest.0DE376A751A13FE2.title: "Goods Over Time"
	quest.0E6662C6387F4D51.quest_desc: ["a pickaxe whose head is shaped as the prospector variant. it still digs like a pickaxe. right click a block: glints in each borne metal's colour, gray dust if there is none. right click in the air pings ore. a finer point gives more glints and wears faster, because everything good is fragile."]
	quest.0E6662C6387F4D51.title: "Prospector's Pick"
	quest.0E77DA85BBAA3E74.quest_desc: ["open the chaos tree and learn a node. rend is the root. later nodes need their prerequisites first; even chaos has paperwork."]
	quest.0E77DA85BBAA3E74.quest_subtitle: "Learn your first node."
	quest.0E77DA85BBAA3E74.title: "Chaos: First Node"
	quest.0E86245A9F97365C.quest_desc: ["&6&lmaterials treatise i: machine-shop consumables&r. opens rolls, wire dies, lathe bits, drill bits, abrasive wheels, saw and plasma heads, calipers. everything in the shop that wears out and wants replacing, which is everything." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.0E86245A9F97365C.title: "Materials Treatise I"
	quest.0E9B8FE5E6E6E428.quest_desc: ["grow sculk in a &6&lculture dish&r fed xp and breathable gas. oxygen from an electrolyser front face works best." "" "warning: a ripe culture left unharvested eventually buds a shrieker set to summon a warden. harvest your pet project before it gets ideas."]
	quest.0E9B8FE5E6E6E428.title: "Culture Dish"
	quest.0ECF1FE023D6A2AC.quest_desc: ["a &6&lmechanical hammer&r does the swinging for you. it needs a crank linkage right behind it and a hammer head seated in it. it draws a lot of power, so a hand crank will not do." "" "warning: machines do not know when they are done. a hammer keeps striking finished output, taking an ingot to plate, to foil, to scrap. it has the enthusiasm of someone who never reads the instructions. take it off in time."]
	quest.0ECF1FE023D6A2AC.title: "The First Real Machine"
	quest.0F3A9B2F40F15721.quest_desc: ["a bracer-slot piece that punches projectiles back faster than they came and lets you parry bare-handed. needs &d&o&nelectrical treatise iii&r: circuits and an engineering table. also a rare find in chests. returning an arrow with interest is its own reward."]
	quest.0F3A9B2F40F15721.title: "Feedbacker"
	quest.0F5BF236A98E59F0.quest_desc: ["open the onslaught tree and learn a node. jab is the root. later nodes need their prerequisites first, so pace yourself, which is an odd thing to say about this tree."]
	quest.0F5BF236A98E59F0.quest_subtitle: "Learn your first node."
	quest.0F5BF236A98E59F0.title: "Onslaught: First Node"
	quest.0F6035C25CF71D6A.quest_desc: ["a warden drops a &6&lculture seed&r and a &6&lrelay organ&r. warning: a warden kills in a few hits. the gift is real, but the giver is not in a sharing mood."]
	quest.0F6035C25CF71D6A.title: "Warden's Gift"
	quest.0F8059EA525EBE2F.quest_desc: ["eat food that was kept cold and is still sound." "" "cold slows spoilage. an ice box or a cold room is how you keep it that way, and how you avoid a sad surprise in the pantry."]
	quest.0F8059EA525EBE2F.title: "Winter Store"
	quest.0FBA1F18B3AD4B99.quest_desc: ["&6&lmechanical treatise i: engines, flywheels and dynamotors&r. opens engines, flywheels and dynamotors, and a long list of machines: steam engine and turbine, mechanical hammer and press, valve, timer, bearings, joints, air and vent valves. it is basically a shopping list with opinions." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.0FBA1F18B3AD4B99.title: "Mechanical Treatise I"
	quest.0FF745C3B7D24C21.quest_desc: ["a cast ingot becomes netherite only by quenching in soul oil while hot. carry it with tongs. a very specific bath for a very specific ingot."]
	quest.0FF745C3B7D24C21.title: "Soul Quench"
	quest.1009C75C5968D50D.quest_desc: ["a shaft only carries work as far as the gears go, and gears have commitment issues. turn rotation into something that travels." "" "a &6&ldynamo&rtor is built from a frame, a winding, a core and a housing, and needs &d&o&nmechanical treatise i&r. sneak-right-click it with an empty hand to switch between generator and motor."]
	quest.1009C75C5968D50D.title: "Dynamo"
	quest.10781B34C3C24BC8.quest_desc: ["a rack has no item recipe of its own: draw it at the blueprint table, with a frame of rod stock and shelves of plate stock, and assemble it at the engineering table. the weaker of the two metals sets how much a bay bears, so a pretty frame on tin shelves is a tin rack." "" "it has eight bays. &c&oa load hotter than the shelf stands wears it, and a frame that burns makes a rack that burns.&r"]
	quest.10781B34C3C24BC8.title: "Pallet Rack"
	quest.109B51567D6DD80D.quest_desc: ["&c&oa gas turbine burns fuel at a steady rate for a lot of power, but it cannot light itself.&r another source has to be turning the line first, so someone has to go first. it is not you, but something you built."]
	quest.109B51567D6DD80D.title: "Gas Turbine"
	quest.10A4E51862D9F0AD.quest_desc: ["a fire has a temperature, and a number beats a guess. make a &6&lthermometer&r from glass, copper foil and a brass plate." "" "carry it in your inventory and hot items show their heat in tu. suddenly everything has opinions in numbers."]
	quest.10A4E51862D9F0AD.title: "A Fire You Can Read"
	quest.1175FDCBC833D14D.quest_desc: ["cast iron and an oxidizer give a clean bloom. needs &d&o&nmaterials treatise ii&r. read first, stir later."]
	quest.1175FDCBC833D14D.title: "Puddling Furnace"
	quest.11A62EE014C79BF5.quest_desc: ["a &6&lcoherer clapper&r taps a coherer open again after each spark, so you no longer have to. wire it in and notice what changes."]
	quest.11A62EE014C79BF5.title: "Make a Spark on Purpose"
	quest.11B76452AAC87C22.quest_desc: ["have a villager accept a commission." "" "villagers post daily orders for finished tools, weapons, armor and dishes. right-click an employed villager and read the orders tab. it is a job board with a pulse."]
	quest.11B76452AAC87C22.title: "Piece Work"
	quest.127CF99D498EEF14.quest_desc: ["write an effect in a script that is not yours. the enchanting table writes attunements onto single parts; nothing is rolled, so the dice can stay home."]
	quest.127CF99D498EEF14.title: "Say the Magic Word"
	quest.12C2B88838265C54.quest_desc: ["&d&o&nelectrical treatise ii&r covers coils, magnets, relays and breakers. it does not include volume i, which is rude but true."]
	quest.12C2B88838265C54.title: "Treatise: Coils and Magnets"
	quest.13B4384940F95F8F.quest_desc: ["make &6&lcable&r. a thicker gauge carries more current but costs more copper. wrap it in an insulating material and it becomes safe to touch up to that material's band."]
	quest.13B4384940F95F8F.title: "Lay Some Cable"
	quest.14BEAAFB50388969.quest_desc: ["a wheel is a tire hub inside a body turned by a rotary bearing. a hub fixed to a body with no bearing is not a wheel, it is a decoration." "" "tires are shaped from stock with a tire trait such as rubber. they wear with distance and skidding, so show-offs pay more."]
	quest.14BEAAFB50388969.title: "Wheels"
	quest.14F4F19F812A9F3C.quest_desc: ["&6&lexperience treatise ii: taps&r. opens the ore, trade and smelter taps, catalyst tap and sculk relay. plumbing, but for enthusiasm." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with experience i held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.14F4F19F812A9F3C.title: "Experience Treatise II"
	quest.155958BCB0377DF6.quest_desc: ["a &6&lflywheel&r stores momentum. it evens out jerky strokes and keeps a line turning through a gap, like a friend who keeps the conversation going." "" "it is drawn at a blueprint table, so &d&o&nmechanical treatise i&r comes first. &c&onotice that it strains above its rated speed and wears, though it never bursts, and it is a poor choice on a line you need to stop quickly.&r it does not like being told to stop."]
	quest.155958BCB0377DF6.title: "Smooth Ride"
	quest.157369236735CE43.quest_desc: ["put food to a fire in the open." "" "a campfire warms food the way a pan does. &c&oit is cooked through only once it is, and it burns if left, so do not wander off to admire the sunset.&r"]
	quest.157369236735CE43.title: "Fire at Dusk"
	quest.1594E709C46D0364.quest_desc: ["a &6&ltreatise binder&r in your inventory, or a &6&ltreatise shelf&r touching the table, counts as holding what is inside. &d&o&ntreatises&r stack to sixteen, so your pockets can stop looking like a library fire."]
	quest.1594E709C46D0364.title: "A Place for Your Books"
	quest.16098BC652BF74CF.quest_desc: ["&c&oradiation is stopped by dense material, which is why a lead chest works and a wooden one does not.&r a &6&lsealed liner&r puts lead around a bay, so radioactive goods give off only what lead lets out. a bare bay radiates in full, onto everyone in the aisle." "" "why lead and not iron is a question the geiger counter will answer."]
	quest.16098BC652BF74CF.title: "Sealed Liner"
	quest.161AD7FF69F10E64.quest_desc: ["link the dock with a data connector to a controller. a sensor card on channels 1 to 4 reads the count of the goods in that watch slot, and an actuator pulse on the same channel queues one stack of it. channel 0 holds retrievals off while storing carries on." "" "holding a channel on asks once. it has to turn off and on again to ask again. a stock level that orders its own restock: that is a thermostat for your pantry."]
	quest.161AD7FF69F10E64.title: "The Dock Is a Node"
	quest.1653174F196CF993.quest_desc: ["open the veil tree and learn a node. shadow step is the root. later nodes need their prerequisites first; nobody sneaks past those."]
	quest.1653174F196CF993.quest_subtitle: "Learn your first node."
	quest.1653174F196CF993.title: "Veil: First Node"
	quest.165775E24D7C3853.quest_desc: ["heat a pan and watch it. food does not wait for you, and it has never once been polite about it." "" "set a &6&lskillet&r on a lit fire, lay food in, and lift it off with tongs. &c&oa bare hand on a hot pan burns, which you may remember from earlier.&r"]
	quest.165775E24D7C3853.title: "Sear"
	quest.168AA6C711A09A5B.quest_desc: ["&c&ocarbon comes in a form that marks paper and does not burn in a fire you can build.&r it is the one thing here that does not mind the heat."]
	quest.168AA6C711A09A5B.title: "Soft Carbon"
	quest.16B971BDEB1EA601.quest_desc: ["use a technique from the anchor tree. stand your ground, and ideally keep standing on it."]
	quest.16B971BDEB1EA601.title: "Hold the Line"
	quest.16F50C5464E88E5B.quest_desc: ["touch a live conductor, and walk away from it. preferably upright." "" "&c&oa powered cable shocks anyone who grabs it bare.&r insulation and rated gloves are what stand between you and the current, so consider them friends."]
	quest.16F50C5464E88E5B.title: "Live Wire"
	quest.18300EE5A546A45B.quest_desc: ["a drum on a vertical shaft blends powders and molten metals, and washes ore. needs &d&o&nchemical treatise i&r. it is a very serious washing machine."]
	quest.18300EE5A546A45B.title: "The Mixer"
	quest.18718D11B426AAC1.quest_desc: ["set bricks under a crucible and it catches the pour: four molds at once, or an open pool that sets to a block. notice that it does not know whether the last pour has set. it is optimistic like that."]
	quest.18718D11B426AAC1.title: "Casting Basin"
	quest.1873DFD1D676D245.quest_desc: ["&c&ochemical treatise iii: explosives opens the demolition charge.&r a &6&lcreeper pen&r can make a powder stronger than gunpowder." "" "warning: these hurt you as readily as anything else. the charge has no favourites."]
	quest.1873DFD1D676D245.title: "Demolition"
	quest.187A2D7058F88557.quest_desc: ["a &6&lboiler&r turns water into steam on a fire. it sits on a firebox, over lava or on a heating coil." "" "warning: steam with nowhere to go builds pressure. &c&oa shut boiler on a hot fire will weep, hiss, scald those nearby, and eventually burst with a block-destroying blast.&r you will regret ignoring the hissing. when it hisses, open the line or put out the fire."]
	quest.187A2D7058F88557.title: "Pressure Cooker"
	quest.188F986CFD3165A7.quest_desc: ["stone and wood only. make a fire that stays where you put it, which is already more than most fires manage." "" "   &c&oa campfire is the simplest: it holds a fixed heat, warms and cooks food, and burns whatever you leave on it.&r"]
	quest.188F986CFD3165A7.title: "First Fire"
	quest.190E29F3D38A0E3E.quest_desc: ["a &6&lcrank linkage&r turns a turning shaft into strokes for the machine in front of it. shaft behind, machine in front, like a very orderly queue." "" "right-click toggles the throw: long is gentle, short is hard. gearing the line down trades rate for strength."]
	quest.190E29F3D38A0E3E.title: "Make It Swing"
	quest.1926AF7A701FC7FB.quest_desc: ["&6&lexperience treatise i: orbs and vessels&r. opens the orb absorber, xp meter and crystal holder. finally, somewhere sensible to put all those glowing orbs you keep stepping on." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with electrical ii and chemical i held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.1926AF7A701FC7FB.title: "Experience Treatise I"
	quest.192FBB27B7AB7700.quest_desc: ["ammonia plus an acid makes &6&lfertiliser&r. use it on a growing crop like bone meal." "" "warning: on a fully grown crop it scorches the plant and drops nothing, so harvest first. the wheat is not impressed by your enthusiasm."]
	quest.192FBB27B7AB7700.title: "Fertiliser"
	quest.1959520F5ADC28E4.quest_desc: ["make your first tool or part out of copper, tin, bronze or brass. the &6&lbronze age&r also takes lead, zinc, gold and silver, and the heat chain hangs off it: brass, and air through iron." "" "nothing stops you making an iron tool before a bronze one. the ages are a record, not a gate, so nobody is checking your homework."]
	quest.1959520F5ADC28E4.title: "Bronze Age"
	quest.1961C0C1D7239F85.quest_desc: ["a leyden jar atop two sticks. &c&ocharge it from a charged jar and the next melee hit spends it in shock, knockback and stagger.&r" "" "&c&ohandle it with respect: stored charge shocks.&r a jar on a stick does not care that it was your idea."]
	quest.1961C0C1D7239F85.title: "Jar Baton"
	quest.19640ED92FD7FD48.quest_desc: ["a pinch of &6&lsalt&r in a pot lets the servings tolerate more of what is live in them. the cheapest upgrade in the pack."]
	quest.19640ED92FD7FD48.title: "Salt"
	quest.19843CCBBEEC8D9F.quest_desc: ["Salt, water, air and the oil under the ground"]
	quest.19843CCBBEEC8D9F.title: "Chemistry"
	quest.1A8C0BF1ADA8AF07.quest_desc: ["the scratch reader drags a point across the goods and records how hard they are. what scratches what is a very old test."]
	quest.1A8C0BF1ADA8AF07.title: "Hardness"
	quest.1A96C4BEDB9F42DA.quest_desc: ["machines run until told to stop, and the output suffers. make one stop on its own, like a grown-up." "" "a timer, wound by hand and set by sneak-right-click, switches whatever it touches. it needs &d&o&nmechanical treatise i&r."]
	quest.1A96C4BEDB9F42DA.title: "Stops Itself"
	quest.1A9B8632DD0A6A6D.quest_desc: ["put a creel above a water wheel and it catches fish as it turns, at the cost of some of the power. dinner is not free, but it is cheap."]
	quest.1A9B8632DD0A6A6D.title: "Fish Wheel"
	quest.1AFCFE938B80FB31.quest_desc: ["a &6&lsteam turbine&r spins very fast and drinks steam in quantity. a single small boiler will not keep up. it has the appetite of a teenager."]
	quest.1AFCFE938B80FB31.title: "Steam Turbine"
	quest.1B2AD0EEB6538640.quest_desc: ["take the battery out and seat it in a &6&lcharger&r, or stand in a charging gantry with the suit on. a tiny nap for a big suit."]
	quest.1B2AD0EEB6538640.title: "Charger"
	quest.1B658DC821789202.quest_desc: ["a &6&lthermoelectric generator&r turns a temperature difference across two different metals into current. make one and look for a hot side and a cold side. yes, it cares which is which."]
	quest.1B658DC821789202.title: "Heat to Current"
	quest.1B8B4D8305F1C1A7.quest_desc: ["wood slabs, a crafting table and wrought iron plate make the table where complex things are assembled. tabs for crafting, fit, repair and &d&o&ntreatise&r; hand tools and fasteners go in the slots." "" "some builds need a &d&o&ntreatise&r held. without it the type is simply missing from the list, which is the table's way of being coy."]
	quest.1B8B4D8305F1C1A7.title: "Engineering Table"
	quest.1BAA61B1CDF7452E.quest_desc: ["silica glass, a redstone chromium ingot and liquid teleportant at high heat make a pearl that is not from an enderman. the enderman was not consulted, and has not noticed."]
	quest.1BAA61B1CDF7452E.title: "Synthetic Pearl"
	quest.1BADC7C2557DDAA0.quest_desc: ["melt copper and pour it into a mold to get an ingot. a mold takes the full amount or nothing, so no half measures. an ingot can be knocked out once it has set."]
	quest.1BADC7C2557DDAA0.title: "Copper Ingot"
	quest.1C0067045883D04D.quest_desc: ["get a &6&lpallet rack&r. read its tooltip for bay strength and the heat its shelves stand. a rack with stock in it cannot be taken apart, so empty it first."]
	quest.1C0067045883D04D.title: "A Rack to Fill"
	quest.1C01926EBDFE0F46.quest_desc: ["keep going until you have spent a good handful of points in the anchor tree. some branches are exclusive: choosing one closes its sibling, so read before you learn. the sibling will remember this."]
	quest.1C01926EBDFE0F46.quest_subtitle: "Spend a fair number of points."
	quest.1C01926EBDFE0F46.title: "Anchor: Spend Points"
	quest.1CB4576B1D85EA64.quest_desc: ["wire a &6&lrefrigeration unit&r against a box and it holds near freezing with no ice. it needs the second &d&o&nchemical treatise&r and power. a condenser beside it takes the box to freezing food. the future, but with cables."]
	quest.1CB4576B1D85EA64.title: "Refrigeration"
	quest.1CBF0FE52A1F501F.quest_desc: ["a pack worn on the back. its strap sets how much weight it carries before it slows you, so the strap has the final word."]
	quest.1CBF0FE52A1F501F.title: "Backpack"
	quest.1D0C1024D1B4FF4A.quest_desc: ["sand melts if the fire is hot and the vessel holds. what it gives is clear. a beach, in essence, with a better attitude."]
	quest.1D0C1024D1B4FF4A.title: "Melted Sand"
	quest.1D14816FE224CAFE.quest_desc: ["the last stage runs in a reactor with an arc head against it, with redstone. hold it in a tank; it is what pays for every crossing. think of it as postage, but weirder."]
	quest.1D14816FE224CAFE.title: "Liquid Teleportant"
	quest.1D2380ED4BAE83CD.quest_desc: ["a &6&lreflow oven&r solders several boards at once, which your wrists will appreciate. set on a firebox, it takes up to four. it needs &d&o&nmaterials treatise i&r and &d&o&nelectrical treatise iii&r."]
	quest.1D2380ED4BAE83CD.title: "Reflow Oven"
	quest.1DACE8815CC35CD7.quest_desc: ["&6&lweapons treatise i: blades and heads&r. opens maul, spear and cleaver, plus the knuckleblaster and whiplash. the names alone should tell you how this ends for somebody." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level. weaponsmiths sell all three weapons volumes."]
	quest.1DACE8815CC35CD7.title: "Weapons Treatise I"
	quest.1E03BBE1633DD3C6.quest_desc: ["an unfitted bay holds one kind of stack up to a mass limit, scaled by the rack's strength. pile heavy things on one and see the limit before the shelf does." "" "one trip carries up to 256 Mu and each level climbed counts as two blocks of travel, so near bays and a fast shaft are quicker."]
	quest.1E03BBE1633DD3C6.title: "Plain Bays"
	quest.1EF27A5FEF740A49.quest_desc: ["a &6&ldrill press&r bores plate and pipe. nothing is drilled until you push, or a linkage in front feeds it. fast feed risks binding, so patience pays here."]
	quest.1EF27A5FEF740A49.title: "Drill Press"
	quest.1F1E5C095CE1A706.quest_desc: ["nothing grows in the void, but something lives there. dark and sealed works anywhere, so the void is just a very committed basement."]
	quest.1F1E5C095CE1A706.title: "Empty, Not Unoccupied"
	quest.1F5041895CB19CA5.quest_desc: ["sneak and use to throw a potion. &c&owarning: fire and explosion potions act on you too.&r aim like you mean it, and stand like you doubt it."]
	quest.1F5041895CB19CA5.title: "Splash"
	quest.2017F0A329638C04.quest_desc: ["brute points come from landed blows with a heavy-hitting weapon, or any blow carrying real weight. check the suits line on a weapon tooltip. repeats pay less, and training dummies stop paying. hitting things hard is a career, but not an infinite one." "" "make a note once you hold some points in the brute tree."]
	quest.2017F0A329638C04.quest_subtitle: "Earn your first points."
	quest.2017F0A329638C04.title: "Brute: Earn Points"
	quest.20E47FF76E6E8A28.quest_desc: ["shape a shell from brick at the stonecutter, or from plate at the smithing table. a shell alone in the crafting grid becomes a crucible. notice the wall: thick holds heat, thin heats quickly. pots, it turns out, have physics."]
	quest.20E47FF76E6E8A28.title: "Crucible Shell"
	quest.20F8FB56A622500E.quest_desc: ["throw a steel ingot into water while it is still very hot and it hisses and hardens. carry it with tongs. a too-cool ingot is only cooled, and your dramatic hiss goes to waste."]
	quest.20F8FB56A622500E.title: "Quench"
	quest.2115F16DAA24DD11.quest_desc: ["a &6&lsculk relay&r links things within range through sculk. needs &d&o&nexperience treatise ii&r. gossip, but infrastructure."]
	quest.2115F16DAA24DD11.title: "Sculk Relay"
	quest.21535158B9D7B3F6.quest_desc: ["a &6&lfuel rod&r is stainless plate around uranium. &c&oit burns for a long time.&r spent ones are far worse, so enjoy them while they are new."]
	quest.21535158B9D7B3F6.title: "Fuel"
	quest.218E2FCEB95AAA45.quest_desc: ["&6&lpneumatic tubes&r move &6&lcarrier&rs between &6&ltube station&rs, but need pressure. &c&otake care: past a point, a run of pressurised tube can burst.&r too much enthusiasm and the post office is on fire."]
	quest.218E2FCEB95AAA45.title: "Pneumatic Tubes"
	quest.22582531484754D6.quest_desc: ["most machines here run on rotation, and rotation travels along &6&lshaft&rs. everything touching along a shaft line is one network, sharing its power and its load, like a very small and very mechanical family." "" "make shafts from ingots of a strong enough metal. bronze, iron and steel all qualify. right-click the end of a shaft with another shaft to extend the line."]
	quest.22582531484754D6.quest_subtitle: "Rotation starts with a line of metal"
	quest.22582531484754D6.title: "Something to Turn"
	quest.22970A18DAEFCA2E.quest_desc: ["stare at a creature until it gives something away. reading a target is the root of the observation tree, and what you learn feeds the quests below. rude, but effective."]
	quest.22970A18DAEFCA2E.title: "Size Up"
	quest.23D832ECD1F94909.quest_desc: ["use a technique from the observation tree. read first, then act, like a person with a plan."]
	quest.23D832ECD1F94909.title: "Eyes Open"
	quest.24CB2C17D139EC9E.quest_desc: ["hold iron ore with charcoal in a vessel in the right band and it clots into a bloom full of slag. too hot and it takes carbon and turns to cast iron, which is the wrong kind of overachieving."]
	quest.24CB2C17D139EC9E.title: "Iron Bloom"
	quest.24D1B8114133AE84.quest_desc: ["&6&lweapons treatise ii: firearms&r. opens guns, launchers, crossbows and fluid casters, plus magazines, the ammo belt and the reloading press. things get louder from here." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with weapons i held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level. weaponsmiths sell all three weapons volumes."]
	quest.24D1B8114133AE84.title: "Weapons Treatise II"
	quest.2516CD7B854AE284.quest_desc: ["pressure vessels, boilers, gas tanks, the mixer, the vacuum pump and the flare stack all need &6&lchemical treatise i: pressure vessels&r. clerics sell it; you can also write or research one. see &d&o&nthe treatises&r chapter for all five ways to get a volume. yes, there is homework."]
	quest.2516CD7B854AE284.title: "Chemical Treatise I"
	quest.253C58D34DFE1DE0.quest_desc: ["the heat reader records how hot the goods were when they arrived. since goods cool on the shelf, remember it is a reading from the door."]
	quest.253C58D34DFE1DE0.title: "Temperature"
	quest.25610486151EC877.quest_desc: ["&6&lrobotics treatise ii: robots&r. opens robots, robot arm, beacon and dock, radio mast, tether reel and the auto engineer. congratulations, you are now somebody's employer." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with robotics i held and mechanical ii and electrical iii held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.25610486151EC877.title: "Robotics Treatise II"
	quest.2573A0D7811B5814.quest_desc: ["three villagers of one profession with job sites close together form a &6&lguild&r. it posts a bigger daily order. notice when one forms. they do not send invitations."]
	quest.2573A0D7811B5814.title: "Guild"
	quest.258E356F7448CD82.quest_desc: ["melt iron ore with no charcoal and it comes out &6&lcast iron&r: hard and brittle. a hand hammer can never shape it, so do not even try to be the hero."]
	quest.258E356F7448CD82.title: "Cast Iron"
	quest.25CAA63CC6D2ECD3.quest_desc: ["&c&oput an overspeed trip over a clutch and it opens the line when it runs too fast.&r sneak-right-click to change the spring. think of it as a fuse with a flair for drama." "" "notice that fast sources like turbines will trip the default setting, so expect some tripping early on."]
	quest.25CAA63CC6D2ECD3.title: "Fuse for Rotation"
	quest.25D588153EA2A3C3.quest_desc: ["link several docks to a catalogue desk with the data connector and it lists and orders the stock of all of them at once. each order takes a line of its own in the dock's queue."]
	quest.25D588153EA2A3C3.title: "Catalog Desk"
	quest.261444A6A443C8B0.quest_desc: ["water is what spoils food. take enough of it away and the food outlasts the season." "" "hang food on a &6&ldrying rack&r under a roof. rain stops the drying, and raw food dried is still raw inside. jerky does not fix everything."]
	quest.261444A6A443C8B0.title: "Keeps"
	quest.265735852860E161.quest_desc: ["a &6&lslider joint&r gives a mount some give so a vehicle does not rattle itself apart. &c&oshock absorption, but for builds with feelings.&r"]
	quest.265735852860E161.title: "Suspension"
	quest.26D83E436C4FFF2B.quest_desc: ["steel fails at heat and wear. press and sinter something harder. steel has limits, and now you get to find them."]
	quest.26D83E436C4FFF2B.title: "A Hard Part"
	quest.26E443E74B2147A2.quest_desc: ["three bricks in an l shape, applied to a crucible or furnace. slower to heat and cool, steadier, and not hotter. reliable, a little dull, very useful."]
	quest.26E443E74B2147A2.title: "Refractory Lining"
	quest.270563B159311C6F.quest_desc: ["spend a read on one large blow and land it. a read is a promise: you looked, now commit. no take-backs, no sheepish shrugging afterward."]
	quest.270563B159311C6F.title: "Exploit"
	quest.272288A25D096D7A.quest_desc: ["hydrochloric acid comes from hydrogen and chlorine. sulfuric acid needs sulfur dioxide, which you get by roasting &6&lpyrite&r. make one of each and note which catalyst bed the second wants. keep your fingers out of both."]
	quest.272288A25D096D7A.title: "Acids"
	quest.274A70BF69817C9F.quest_desc: ["a &6&lpressure gauge&r tells you how close a boiler is to its limit. fit one before you trust a fire. optimism is not a safety device."]
	quest.274A70BF69817C9F.title: "Read the Pressure"
	quest.275202100E7B1E4B.quest_desc: ["some metal melts in a cooler fire than copper and stays bright. find it in the ground and melt it. it is shy about being found."]
	quest.275202100E7B1E4B.title: "Soft and Silvery"
	quest.278ADDD048D0FED5.quest_desc: ["place the three parts side by side in a crafting grid to make a &6&ltelescope&r. assembly is mercifully short."]
	quest.278ADDD048D0FED5.title: "Telescope"
	quest.28456B87CBE72CEC.quest_desc: ["keep going until you have spent a good handful of points in the chaos tree. some branches are exclusive: choosing one closes its sibling, so read before you learn. a rare case where the careful option is the fun one."]
	quest.28456B87CBE72CEC.quest_subtitle: "Spend a fair number of points."
	quest.28456B87CBE72CEC.title: "Chaos: Spend Points"
	quest.291F355288A55856.quest_desc: ["a chest that keeps food cold for as long as it has ice. without ice it is just a chest, and a smug one."]
	quest.291F355288A55856.title: "Ice Box"
	quest.2949F54C63C68B4B.quest_desc: ["&6&lweapons treatise iii: electric guns&r. opens electric guns. the same idea as before, but with lightning and worse manners." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with weapons ii held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level. weaponsmiths sell all three weapons volumes."]
	quest.2949F54C63C68B4B.title: "Weapons Treatise III"
	quest.2984609CA157C059.quest_desc: ["&c&oa leyden jar holds charge and releases it as a burst.&r charge leaks away on its own, so use it soon, before it loses interest." "" "   &c&owarning: a jar rated mv or above shocks you while charged, and a jar fed a band above its rating cracks and shocks everything nearby.&r"]
	quest.2984609CA157C059.title: "Store the Charge"
	quest.29F505259DD46349.quest_desc: ["some food wants hours and more than one ingredient. patience, as a recipe." "" "a &6&lstockpot&r cooks a batch as one mixture. while there is water it stays at boiling; boil it dry and it climbs fast. so top it up, or watch it become a problem."]
	quest.29F505259DD46349.title: "Slow Simmer"
	quest.2A33FE8D79515479.quest_desc: ["there is no iron sword, only a blade of one metal on a grip of another. shape a head at the smithing table, a handle at the woodworking table (or a stone head at the stonecutter), add a binding, and put them together in the crafting grid." "" "pick the pieces for what they are made of: hardness, mass and balance decide what the tool does. yes, there is homework."]
	quest.2A33FE8D79515479.title: "A Head on a Handle"
	quest.2A506440198D8ACC.quest_desc: ["a &6&llaser&r seats a crystal that lases, such as ruby, and wants an mv line. &c&oswitched on, by a controller switch card or redstone, it fires a beam that cuts blocks by hardness and burns whatever lives in it.&r switched off, it only measures the distance ahead." "" "notice that the crystal heats while it fires and cracks if you push it, so hard cuts are done in pulses. made at the engineering table, and it needs electrical school 3."]
	quest.2A506440198D8ACC.title: "Light, Pumped"
	quest.2A6AB12936D97AE4.quest_desc: ["an &6&lelectroscope&r tells you the band of a line and a &6&lgalvanometer&r its current. neither is required, but guessing on a live line is how you get hurt." "" "&c&owarning: touching either to a bare live wire shocks you.&r the tool is not a magic wand."]
	quest.2A6AB12936D97AE4.title: "Meter Everything"
	quest.2A7C1AE7ABA3D9A6.quest_desc: ["&6&lnuclear treatise i: reactors and fuel&r. opens the gas centrifuge, the chemical reactor, the fission reactor core and fuel rods. read it with respect, and possibly from a distance." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with chemical ii and electrical ii held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.2A7C1AE7ABA3D9A6.title: "Nuclear Treatise I"
	quest.2A91852D562C237F.quest_desc: ["a barbed spear on a lanyard from the wrist. needs &d&o&nweapons treatise i&r: blades and heads. it comes back, which is more than can be said for most borrowed tools."]
	quest.2A91852D562C237F.title: "Whiplash"
	quest.2AE380C7E24931FD.quest_desc: ["boilers are modular and drawn at a blueprint table. &d&o&nchemical treatise i&r covers boilers, &6&lpressure vessels&r and gas tanks. read it before the part where things get loud."]
	quest.2AE380C7E24931FD.title: "Pressure Vessels"
	quest.2B6B93A9B2CF4769.quest_desc: ["ordinary brick cracks in a hot fire. a particular clay, fired hard, does not. some bricks just have their life together."]
	quest.2B6B93A9B2CF4769.title: "Brick That Does Not Burn"
	quest.2B9AA1F5DF1C9C5B.quest_desc: ["thaumaturge-dependent. a relief valve with a gauge for essentia stores; it opens when the store is nearly full. empty-hand click to read it, since the gauge is shy."]
	quest.2B9AA1F5DF1C9C5B.title: "Essentia Vent (Thaumaturge)"
	quest.2BDB553829E5C234.quest_desc: ["steam is heavy for its power. &c&oburn something refined inside the machine instead.&r" "" "engines are built from a block, pistons, crankshaft, spark plug and head. match the cylinder head's compression to the fuel: the wrong pairing misfires or knocks and wears the engine, and a knocking engine is not a polite visitor."]
	quest.2BDB553829E5C234.title: "Heat Engine"
	quest.2C349A27B29FDEF0.quest_desc: ["anchor points come from landing a parry (g), once per attacker. timing beats armor. repeats pay less, and training dummies stop paying, having apparently unionized." "" "make a note once you hold some points in the anchor tree, preferably a mental one."]
	quest.2C349A27B29FDEF0.quest_subtitle: "Earn your first points."
	quest.2C349A27B29FDEF0.title: "Anchor: Earn Points"
	quest.2C4866A70BAB0533.quest_desc: ["exosuit upgrades are modules built from casing, wiring and attachments: optic, filter, thermal, plating, actuator, spring, tread, thruster, coil, dispenser. needs &d&o&nrobotics treatise i&r: &6&lsuit module&rs. it reads like a shopping list for a very odd shopper."]
	quest.2C4866A70BAB0533.title: "Suit Module"
	quest.2C5DAA4A49E4E758.quest_desc: ["hold a sharp telescope on a planet on a clear night and see it as a disc. a small disc, but a real one." "" "keep the planet in the middle of the view. planets come back on their own schedule, so be patient. they are not on your clock."]
	quest.2C5DAA4A49E4E758.title: "A Light That Wanders"
	quest.2C62FA0FBDED5E34.quest_desc: ["keep going until you have spent a good handful of points in the proficiency tree. some branches are exclusive: choosing one closes its sibling, so read before you learn. sensible people tend to anyway."]
	quest.2C62FA0FBDED5E34.quest_subtitle: "Spend a fair number of points."
	quest.2C62FA0FBDED5E34.title: "Proficiency: Spend Points"
	quest.2D3F71D5384F4425.quest_desc: ["a &6&lbattery&r stores what a generator makes and gives it back when the line is quiet, like a very small squirrel with a very large acorn. build one from plates and a case." "" "&c&owarning: lead-acid cells gas hydrogen when overcharged, lithium types can run away into a fire, and a charged battery with a high-band case will shock you.&r batteries are polite until they are not."]
	quest.2D3F71D5384F4425.title: "Reserve Power"
	quest.2DACEF5CF419D095.quest_desc: ["mail is not the same as being there. go to where the port sends, and see what the parcel has been up to."]
	quest.2DACEF5CF419D095.title: "Out of Reach"
	quest.2E14DB83146FA5EE.quest_desc: ["a &6&lpivot mast&r carries an arm with a tip that cuts, breaks, strikes, plants, feeds or collects. &c&omind the striking tip: it hurts players, and that includes you, so stand somewhere else.&r"]
	quest.2E14DB83146FA5EE.title: "Pivot Mast"
	quest.2E33F9041D89DCFD.quest_desc: ["open the observation tree and learn a node. size up is the root. later nodes need their prerequisites first, which you would have noticed if you were reading closely."]
	quest.2E33F9041D89DCFD.quest_subtitle: "Learn your first node."
	quest.2E33F9041D89DCFD.title: "Observation: First Node"
	quest.2E49B0EFB9F57DDC.quest_desc: ["a machine that repeats one assembly you made by hand at the engineering table. record the craft onto a recipe data stick, then let it replay. needs &d&o&nrobotics treatise ii&r: robots." "" "it draws serious power and wears its own tools. like an intern, but with better time management."]
	quest.2E49B0EFB9F57DDC.title: "Auto Engineer"
	quest.2EE07D46B34EB1AF.quest_desc: ["take a blow wearing a full outfit of armor you built: helmet, chestplate, leggings and boots. yes, all four. the boots count, even though nobody ever aims at the boots."]
	quest.2EE07D46B34EB1AF.title: "Head to Toe"
	quest.2F0D4EA98BD3FE00.quest_desc: ["metals will not dissolve in water. a reactor and an acid might. the reactor is a &d&o&nnuclear treatise i&r item despite being chemical, which is just how the filing system works here. it knows no recipes: heat it, feed it, and read the reaction table." "" "&c&owarning: it bursts at high pressure, and too much heat makes worse products, not better.&r more is not always more."]
	quest.2F0D4EA98BD3FE00.title: "Something to React In"
	quest.2FFEE5651FBA9F68.quest_desc: ["hammer a copper ingot into a plate. let go in time; the next stage is foil, and foil is where plates go to be disappointing."]
	quest.2FFEE5651FBA9F68.title: "Copper Plate"
	quest.302FC6319252EE02.quest_desc: ["write one by taking apart a specimen at the &6&lengineering table&r &d&o&ntreatise&r tab, research one at the &6&lresearch table&r, find one rarely in dungeon, mineshaft, desert temple, stronghold or bastion chests, sight a planet for aerospace iv, or buy one from a villager. knowledge is earned, never handed out by a level, so the grind is the point."]
	quest.302FC6319252EE02.title: "Five Ways to a Volume"
	quest.30A38593274786FF.quest_desc: ["spent rods are about ten times as radioactive as fresh. make a &6&lspent fuel pool&r, keep it topped up, and keep spent rods in lead." "" "warning: a dry pool is extremely radioactive and rods in it melt to slag. check the water like it is a houseplant." "" "spent rods are not only waste. a thermal vessel with hydrochloric acid dissolves one into plutonium."]
	quest.30A38593274786FF.title: "Spent Fuel"
	quest.30AAC9DE9C6AEC18.quest_desc: ["many parts want a &d&o&ntreatise&r on the shelf before you can draw or assemble them. &d&o&ntreatises&r are kept, never used up, and each volume stands alone, so no cliffhangers." "" "&6&lmechanical treatise i&r covers engines, flywheels, bearings, clutches, the steam engine, the mechanical hammer and press, and the machines of the shop. it is a lot of reading for a book about spinning things."]
	quest.30AAC9DE9C6AEC18.title: "Mechanical Treatise I"
	quest.30BCCB533161179C.quest_desc: ["make a &6&lgas tank&r. &c&ohoop bands and a relief valve can be fitted as add-ons, and a compressor can fill a tank past its danger line.&r note what happens if you try. it is educational, in the way a dropped anvil is educational."]
	quest.30BCCB533161179C.title: "Hold the Gas"
	quest.30E9A04098C3398A.quest_desc: ["when the machine is too far for a shaft, a &6&lbelt&r between two pulleys carries the turning instead. the long-distance relationship of mechanics." "" "a belt only carries so much. past that it slips, so the driven side slows down. slipping is also what wears a belt out, so it is not a free lunch."]
	quest.30E9A04098C3398A.title: "Belts, Not Shafts"
	quest.30EF2F72EE3A2D0C.quest_desc: ["the machine-shop consumables, rolls, wire dies, lathe bits, drill bits and abrasive wheels, come from &6&lmaterials treatise i&r. the lathe, drill press, rolling mill and wire drawer need both this and &d&o&nmechanical treatise i&r. yes, homework again."]
	quest.30EF2F72EE3A2D0C.title: "Materials Treatise I"
	quest.31DA700788582C28.quest_desc: ["raw is no good and black is worse. take it off at the moment between." "" "raw food can carry something live. cooked through is safe, kept on it dries out, and hotter still it chars. the window is narrow and it is on a timer."]
	quest.31DA700788582C28.title: "Just Right"
	quest.3252873A0727ED8B.quest_desc: ["modules fitted to the dock, one per face, read goods on their way in and record the result with the goods. that record stays with them in their bay until a later delivery overwrites it. heads have the weaknesses they have on a belt and misread near a band edge, and a second head on the same property lowers the chance of a mistake." "" "some heads need an LV wire against the dock. optical readers and screens foul and want wiping."]
	quest.3252873A0727ED8B.title: "Reader Heads"
	quest.32BFCABBAAABE490.quest_desc: ["use a technique from the chaos tree. leave them with what you did, plus a little something to talk about."]
	quest.32BFCABBAAABE490.title: "Leave a Mark"
	quest.334FD6300216DB92.quest_desc: ["a &6&lshield&r is six faces and a rim. a small face makes a buckler that parries; a large rectangular one makes a tower shield; a kite-shaped face turns arrows and bolts back. these are builds, not separate items, so the shield shop is you."]
	quest.334FD6300216DB92.title: "Guard Up"
	quest.33A0B7C4227EE7B4.quest_desc: ["set against a crucible side; open ones double the heat loss. needs &d&o&nmechanical treatise i&r. think of it as a window you can leave open on purpose."]
	quest.33A0B7C4227EE7B4.title: "Damper"
	quest.34CCDE9AF11F7811.quest_desc: ["a pallet bay stacks things, and stacking forgets. a cabinet holds up to 16 single pieces of any item and each keeps its own wear and charge. a worn tool goes in worn and comes out worn."]
	quest.34CCDE9AF11F7811.title: "Keeping State"
	quest.351A81894454C177.quest_desc: ["&c&ohydrogen lifts but burns.&r helium does not. build a gas cell and fill it, and choose with the confidence of someone who read the last two entries."]
	quest.351A81894454C177.title: "Lighter than Air"
	quest.3542565DE58225E0.quest_desc: ["paper, an ink sac and an iron nugget make an &6&lunlearning token&r. use it to respec a tree you regret. every build has one of those."]
	quest.3542565DE58225E0.title: "Change Your Mind"
	quest.35919F58D52D0DEC.quest_desc: ["open the brute tree and learn a node. grab is the root: take hold of what you hit. later nodes need their prerequisites first, and no amount of shoving changes that."]
	quest.35919F58D52D0DEC.quest_subtitle: "Learn your first node."
	quest.35919F58D52D0DEC.title: "Brute: First Node"
	quest.35DF9258637F1466.quest_desc: ["hammer-forge a &6&lwrench&r in the grid from hot ingots of one metal. a hard enough one turns a block a quarter turn on right-click. it is a lot of effort for a quarter turn, but it is your quarter turn."]
	quest.35DF9258637F1466.title: "Turn It a Quarter"
	quest.36D2C6C169B2EAFE.quest_desc: ["chorus fruit and water in the reactor give a raw spatial slurry. it is the first of four stages toward liquid teleportant, so do not get attached."]
	quest.36D2C6C169B2EAFE.title: "Raw Slurry"
	quest.374B91B768A44597.quest_desc: ["a &6&ltuned eye&r finds a port's partner. useful when you have forgotten where you put it, which is a normal thing to forget."]
	quest.374B91B768A44597.title: "Tuned Eye"
	quest.380B5FD56F79044C.quest_desc: ["Brewing, experience, enchanting and Thaumaturge"]
	quest.380B5FD56F79044C.title: "Magic and Experience"
	quest.388B901EFC2DE7E6.quest_desc: ["hand-made things cannot &6&llift&r themselves, however much they believe in themselves." "" "a thruster needs &d&o&naerospace treatise ii&r. it needs air for oxygen, so it does not work in the end or under water, and it does nothing unless the craft is lifted."]
	quest.388B901EFC2DE7E6.title: "Lift"
	quest.38A44D8D5FD41DC8.quest_desc: ["use a technique from the proficiency tree. get out of trouble, ideally the trouble you got yourself into."]
	quest.38A44D8D5FD41DC8.title: "Still Standing"
	quest.38BC80D81A1F050B.quest_desc: ["a bow is built from three limbs and three lengths of string. its draw is something skeletons telegraph and you can read, so consider it a courtesy and return it."]
	quest.38BC80D81A1F050B.title: "Draw and Loose"
	quest.38ED576FA330BEB4.quest_desc: ["&6&lcable&r carries current and does not care who touches it. it has no favourites. treat any powered line as bare until you know otherwise."]
	quest.38ED576FA330BEB4.title: "A Live Line"
	quest.39346E556F3C760A.quest_desc: ["fix a grapple line on something and let it bite." "" "a line is only as good as what it is fixed to. choose your anchor like you choose your friends."]
	quest.39346E556F3C760A.title: "Taking Hold"
	quest.399833097802EC90.quest_desc: ["the weapon of the time &6&lbefore real guns&r: a smoothbore barrel, a receiver, a trigger, a grip and a lock. it needs no blueprint, and roughly one pull in eight only flashes in the pan. consider that one in eight a character trait." "" "&c&opowder burns.&r expect it to bite back."]
	quest.399833097802EC90.title: "Before Real Guns"
	quest.399EB91A5623D3EF.quest_desc: ["food rots by the clock and a rack keeps the clock running. a &6&lcold plate fitting&r only conducts: copper carries heat away, but it needs somewhere to put it, which is a running refrigeration unit touching or cooling the rack." "" "with no running unit the bay spoils at the room's rate and looks fine until opened. a &6&lcold plate&r with no pump is a decorative copper shelf."]
	quest.399EB91A5623D3EF.title: "Cold Plate"
	quest.39AC4729F0735B1F.quest_desc: ["a pair of &6&ltongs&r lets you lift hot work and hot pans without a bare hand on them. they are a pair of long fingers that do not mind."]
	quest.39AC4729F0735B1F.title: "Tongs"
	quest.3A1297392ACAD267.quest_desc: ["leather, planks and a shaft, set against the firebox and driven by a &6&lcrank linkage&r. air raises a fire's heat but does not make the fuel last longer. it runs whenever the shaft turns, whether you are watching or not."]
	quest.3A1297392ACAD267.title: "Bellows"
	quest.3A983FCC14404DB3.quest_desc: ["lift or carry something too hot for bare skin, with tongs or gloves between you and it." "" "&c&oa glowing piece burns bare hands, and you will only need to learn that once.&r tongs are two rods, a grip and a hammer in the crafting grid."]
	quest.3A983FCC14404DB3.title: "Cool Hand"
	quest.3AA6D8D044E466A7.quest_desc: ["a &6&lrolling mill&r takes ingots to rods and plates to pipes, and presses one plate onto another. brittle stock grinds to dust, which is a rude way to find out it was brittle."]
	quest.3AA6D8D044E466A7.title: "Rolling Mill"
	quest.3B1368368B9BFE0C.quest_desc: ["a &6&lbreaker&r trips at its gauge's rating and lets you cut a line by hand. opening one under heavy current costs it condition." "" "&c&owarning: at the very highest bands, opening a breaker under load throws an arc flash that burns and ignites everything living within a few blocks.&r that includes you, and your opinion of breakers."]
	quest.3B1368368B9BFE0C.title: "Cut It Off"
	quest.3B15B7A6610DB1B4.quest_desc: ["a small battery-powered crawler built from a chassis, a drive and a tool head. it needs a battery and a punch card with its program. needs &6&lrobot&rics &d&o&ntreatise ii&r: &6&lrobot&rs. it is small, earnest and not very bright."]
	quest.3B15B7A6610DB1B4.title: "Robot"
	quest.3B54FD369A3E9261.quest_desc: ["paper and crafting tables make the table where drawings are made. it shows a build's figures before you commit to it, and blueprints can be copied. a village house chest will now and then hold a ready-made starter design, if you would rather not trade for one. measure twice, craft once."]
	quest.3B54FD369A3E9261.title: "Blueprint Table"
	quest.3B598DAAC1C01146.quest_desc: ["with no &6&ltrade tap&r within reach, a counter pays no experience at all. you get the coins of the sale, but not the sparkle."]
	quest.3B598DAAC1C01146.title: "Trade Tap"
	quest.3BD49727B6A0EE3B.quest_desc: ["a &6&lwire drawer&r draws rod into wire, and makes welding rods. fast draws can snap the wire and ruin the piece, but some metals can only be drawn fast. so some days you gamble."]
	quest.3BD49727B6A0EE3B.title: "Wire Drawer"
	quest.3C2289E89E9544E2.quest_desc: ["writes &d&o&ntreatises&r and rites for 40 experience points each. a library card, priced in levels."]
	quest.3C2289E89E9544E2.title: "Research Table"
	quest.3C5E85837AB7B4DC.quest_desc: ["wear a pack heavier than it is rated for, and feel it. you will feel it." "" "over the rating you are slower and cannot sprint, and the strap wears until it lets go. watch the strap, because it will not warn you politely."]
	quest.3C5E85837AB7B4DC.title: "Pack Mule"
	quest.3C8813C6BB21800B.quest_desc: ["be at a market cross when the market opens." "" "the wandering trader sets up there, and villagers nearby want more. a crowd is good for business and bad for personal space."]
	quest.3C8813C6BB21800B.title: "Market Day"
	quest.3CC3F20B7243EAE4.quest_desc: ["netherite can be made without scrap: a powder pressed to a green compact and sintered under nitrogen. the long way round, but nobody has to go digging."]
	quest.3CC3F20B7243EAE4.title: "Synthesized"
	quest.3CC9EF1F0629AD09.quest_desc: ["a winch fitting for the grapple, built at the engineering table. needs &d&o&nmechanical treatise i&r: engines, flywheels and dynamotors. the crank is optional; &d&o&nthe treatise&r is not."]
	quest.3CC9EF1F0629AD09.title: "Grapple Winch"
	quest.3D1A0ED62BBA014F.quest_desc: ["a &6&lpowered bellows&r is one way to push air into a vessel. fit a &6&lpressure gauge&r so you can read what you are doing instead of guessing. guessing is how the last vessel got its dramatic exit."]
	quest.3D1A0ED62BBA014F.title: "Something to Squeeze With"
	quest.3D753DCD6565FF5B.quest_desc: ["a modular tool: shape the blade hot, then fit a handle. the blade's material sets how long it lasts. the sharper end is the important end."]
	quest.3D753DCD6565FF5B.title: "Hand Knife"
	quest.3DAF30BF7984C37D.quest_desc: ["a &6&lcatalyst tap&r draws experience from a sculk catalyst. needs &d&o&nexperience treatise ii&r. you are, politely, milking a sculk catalyst."]
	quest.3DAF30BF7984C37D.title: "Catalyst Tap"
	quest.3DB4F595FC177F18.quest_desc: ["a pillar for a paved square. it counts only on an open square of paving. a lawn will not impress it."]
	quest.3DB4F595FC177F18.title: "Market Cross"
	quest.3DBAA307E2DEF9E1.quest_desc: ["&d&o&nnuclear treatise i&r covers reactors, fuel and enrichment. studying it needs &d&o&nchemical treatise ii&r and &d&o&nelectrical treatise ii&r held. light reading, with prerequisites."]
	quest.3DBAA307E2DEF9E1.title: "Treatise: Reactors and Fuel"
	quest.3DD80F2973F8178B.quest_desc: ["&6&lthe lift&r picks up a build and makes it a single moving thing. build on top of it so that it touches nothing else, then right-click to &6&llift&r. a lifted build can be set down again as blocks, so nothing is permanent, least of all your mistakes."]
	quest.3DD80F2973F8178B.title: "The Lift"
	quest.3DFF5CDCFF5BDE56.quest_desc: ["some reactions only go when squeezed, much like some people. make a pressure vessel and contain it, and leave it a way out. &c&owarning: pump too much in and it bursts.&r it will not be gentle about it."]
	quest.3DFF5CDCFF5BDE56.title: "Under Pressure"
	quest.3E306A1468ED2279.quest_desc: ["a &6&lvacuum dryer&r turns a potion into crystals that keep. needs &d&o&nchemical treatise ii&r. warning: it scorches above its limit, so no cranking it to see what happens."]
	quest.3E306A1468ED2279.title: "Potion Salts"
	quest.3E5A9F220E315BE6.quest_desc: ["machine heads are drawn at a blueprint table, shaped at a smithing table and put together in a crafting grid. three stations for one little head." "" "misuse wears the head, not the machine, which is generous of it. the edge must be harder than what it cuts."]
	quest.3E5A9F220E315BE6.title: "Rolls and Dies"
	quest.3E772FCE1BE2AB3C.quest_desc: ["a &6&ldosimeter&r keeps a running dose. a rate means little by itself; what matters is rate times time. loitering has a price."]
	quest.3E772FCE1BE2AB3C.title: "Dosimeter"
	quest.3F60BA8D27ACE616.quest_desc: ["thaumaturge-dependent. turns essentia from a store into gas, one way only. no returns. needs &d&o&nmechanical treatise i&r."]
	quest.3F60BA8D27ACE616.title: "Essentia Adapter (Thaumaturge)"
	quest.3F986C8C5899A97A.quest_desc: ["hit armor with a weapon harder than what it wears, and let it show. material choice is a weapon choice, so the smugness is earned."]
	quest.3F986C8C5899A97A.title: "Right Tool"
	quest.3F9ED06D0896AD3A.quest_desc: ["a &6&lcharge&r is the powder behind a bullet. gunpowder and blaze powder cook off at different heats, which matters in a hot barrel. pick the one that suits your barrel's temperament."]
	quest.3F9ED06D0896AD3A.title: "Charge"
	quest.4032F6CA1B16E086.quest_desc: ["veil points come from a roll that dodged a blow, and from striking something that has not noticed you. quiet footsteps trickle in too. repeats pay less, and training dummies stop paying. they notice nothing, which sounds like a loophole and is not." "" "make a note once you hold some points in the veil tree, discreetly."]
	quest.4032F6CA1B16E086.quest_subtitle: "Earn your first points."
	quest.4032F6CA1B16E086.title: "Veil: Earn Points"
	quest.409144DDD0AEDF57.quest_desc: ["&c&oa radiation sensor reads the local rate and hands it to a controller, so a machine can react to it.&r uranium glass also glows as a rough visible dosimeter, a nightlight with a past."]
	quest.409144DDD0AEDF57.title: "Sensing Radiation"
	quest.41370EDD8F570279.quest_desc: ["dense material shields. ordinary chests do not, but a &6&llead chest&r does, which makes it the world's heaviest coat closet. carry sources in your hands and store them behind lead."]
	quest.41370EDD8F570279.title: "Lead Lining"
	quest.41A1CD64EE354712.quest_desc: ["finish a fight with a blade or barrel whose edge runs hot. heat is a figure too, and some weapons carry it, so treat them accordingly."]
	quest.41A1CD64EE354712.title: "Hot Edge"
	quest.41C2D8147187DAF1.quest_desc: ["a &6&lgearbox&r joins shafts on any of its six faces at the same speed. opposite faces turn opposite ways, so do not take it personally when one side spins away from you." "" "it is built from steel plate, cogs and a shaft with machine bolts, so it also needs &d&o&nmechanical treatise ii&r."]
	quest.41C2D8147187DAF1.title: "Gearbox"
	quest.41CB250A07BD36AF.quest_desc: ["get &6&la timer&r. notice how long it runs after a wind, and what it can switch: clutches, valves and breakers among them. a tiny clockwork boss."]
	quest.41CB250A07BD36AF.title: "A Timer"
	quest.42077C44CFE51F02.quest_desc: ["stack a &6&lreboiler&r, heated from below, with at least one &6&lcolumn tray&r. crude splits by boiling point into naphtha, kerosene and diesel." "" "warning: an open hot vessel past the flash point makes a flash fire. close the lid, or enjoy the eyebrow situation."]
	quest.42077C44CFE51F02.title: "Distillation"
	quest.42AC0F1CD6F05B2A.quest_desc: ["a derrick bores down to the basin. the &6&lderrick base&r comes from &d&o&nmechanical treatise ii&r: transmission. choke the &6&lwellhead&r as you like, but note that drawing too hard cones the basin. the ground has feelings about being sucked dry."]
	quest.42AC0F1CD6F05B2A.title: "Real Extraction"
	quest.42AFB04516F010FE.quest_desc: ["a &6&lgrapple&r and a winch put a line where you want it. a very pointy way of saying hello to a wall."]
	quest.42AFB04516F010FE.title: "Grapple"
	quest.42BB5C06C39AC9A6.quest_desc: ["a mechanical arm. a companion piece for robots and a part of the auto engineer. it has no hands, but it has a lot of reach."]
	quest.42BB5C06C39AC9A6.title: "Robot Arm"
	quest.42C1BFBB7C4FC482.quest_desc: ["a carriage runs on &6&lwarehouse rail&r in a straight line behind the dock, up to 64 long, with racks stood against either side. the &6&lshuttle head&r drives it, and it must face away from the dock." "" "turn the head with a shaft. the carriage's speed follows the shaft's speed in either direction, and a still shaft parks it. a heavy load loads the shaft harder the faster it turns, so a weak source slows under it."]
	quest.42C1BFBB7C4FC482.title: "Rail and Shuttle"
	quest.42D94BFB11145303.quest_desc: ["gas you cannot use has to go somewhere, and that somewhere is a tall chimney with opinions. &c&oa flare stack burns it off.&r &c&owarning: burning hydrogen and fuel vapors is still fire, so do not stand close and admire it.&r"]
	quest.42D94BFB11145303.title: "A Safe Vent"
	quest.42EB53090F7D4157.quest_desc: ["a glowstone &6&llamp&r turns current into light. &c&onotice that too little current dims it and too much burns it out at once, so it has exactly two moods.&r it needs no &d&o&ntreatise&r."]
	quest.42EB53090F7D4157.title: "Let There Be Light"
	quest.43390F7CEE15258A.quest_desc: ["some ores will not smelt, and no amount of glaring helps. electricity can reduce them. dissolve bauxite in lye in the reactor for &6&lalumina&r, then it goes into a molten cryolite bath in the electrolyser." "" "warning: with no alumina in the bath the cell suffers the anode effect and is damaged. feed the bath."]
	quest.43390F7CEE15258A.title: "Bauxite Gives Way"
	quest.437513F68489B775.quest_desc: ["thaumaturge-dependent: it does nothing without that mod. a &6&lvis tap&r turns vis from a thaumaturge relay into medium voltage current." "" "warning: left running with nothing connected it fouls the aura with flux. needs &d&o&nelectrical treatise ii&r."]
	quest.437513F68489B775.title: "Vis Tap (Thaumaturge)"
	quest.43DA2EA1811B681A.quest_desc: ["iron with a little carbon, melted clean. &c&othe band is narrow and a fresh melt burns above it.&r notice that a light crucible on a blown fire climbs too fast; mass and lining slow it. fast is not always good."]
	quest.43DA2EA1811B681A.title: "Steel in the Crucible"
	quest.43E390E6CBD85FD7.quest_desc: ["hold to stir, tap to skim. a very small job done with great authority."]
	quest.43E390E6CBD85FD7.title: "Spoon"
	quest.44057A14D1D520E9.quest_desc: ["chlorine plus lye gives hypochlorite bleach. dip dyed wool, concrete powder or a banner in it, and watch the colour give up." "" "&c&owarning: chlorine is toxic.&r the bleach is the polite half of the family."]
	quest.44057A14D1D520E9.title: "Bleach It White"
	quest.4436A699651A8DFC.quest_desc: ["&6&lchemical treatise ii: heat and compression&r. opens heat exchangers and gas compressors, plus the cryocooler, refrigeration unit and vacuum dryer. hot and cold, both handled with great seriousness." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with chemical i held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level. clerics sell chemical i and ii."]
	quest.4436A699651A8DFC.title: "Chemical Treatise II"
	quest.447C18F90C15CC80.quest_desc: ["plain rock and water hide a lot more than they let on. start with salt: get some, and notice how many later processes begin with a pinch of it dissolved in water. chemistry's opening move is, essentially, soup."]
	quest.447C18F90C15CC80.title: "Salt and Water"
	quest.45EFBFF645CD0C42.quest_desc: ["wall in a space with full blocks and put a unit inside it. everything in the room settles at its temperature. notice where the walls leak, because the cold certainly will."]
	quest.45EFBFF645CD0C42.title: "Cold Room"
	quest.46C278743EDC5F3D.quest_desc: ["plates of one metal plus leather, shapeless, make a &6&lbracer&r for the curios &6&lbracer&r slot. it widens your parry window a little. combat gear appears once you have wrought iron plate. a small upgrade with a big forearm energy."]
	quest.46C278743EDC5F3D.title: "Bracer"
	quest.46E77CCA4D946039.quest_desc: ["the gap is not empty. asteroids of tuff hold iron, pentlandite, sperrylite, osmiridium and the odd rare beryl, and rare derelict iron wrecks drift by with a chest still aboard. look around you."]
	quest.46E77CCA4D946039.title: "Salvage"
	quest.4738E0EFDF12225E.quest_desc: ["a hammer from cobblestone and sticks. hold it in one hand and a workpiece in the other, and hold right-click to swing." "" "a blow weaker than a metal's hardness does nothing, and swinging past a plate turns it to foil, then scrap. enthusiasm is not a plan."]
	quest.4738E0EFDF12225E.title: "A Hand Hammer"
	quest.477D24A280AEDBAB.quest_desc: ["&d&o&nexperience treatise i&r: orbs and &6&lvessels&r opens the &6&lcrystal holder&r. containers come in vial, flask and carboy sizes, which is cosmopolitan for jars."]
	quest.477D24A280AEDBAB.title: "Vessels"
	quest.47BB1F198AC92DB6.quest_desc: ["one program fills a controller. store more than it holds, because ambition has to live somewhere." "" "a &6&lmemory&r drum needs &d&o&nelectrical treatise iii&r."]
	quest.47BB1F198AC92DB6.title: "Memory"
	quest.482E930D62D19277.quest_desc: ["&6&lmaterials treatise ii: metallurgy and heat treatment&r. opens the crude blast furnace, improved and annealing furnaces and the puddling furnace. you will have strong feelings about furnaces by the end." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with materials i held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.482E930D62D19277.title: "Materials Treatise II"
	quest.483635807FBD0F9D.quest_desc: ["gas cells hold lift gas, a &6&lvent valve&r lets it out and a &6&lballast tank&r holds water as weight. a balloon, but with engineering." "" "&c&owarning: hydrogen and some other lift gases burn, and a burning envelope takes the ship with it.&r lift also thins to nothing near the top of the sky, so do not get ambitious."]
	quest.483635807FBD0F9D.title: "Lighter than Air"
	quest.48ABA1210FB734F6.quest_desc: ["the ground itself is hot here, and there is no water. go and see what a fire can do with it." "" "&c&owarning: the nether burns and cannot be quenched.&r bring your optimism, leave your water bucket."]
	quest.48ABA1210FB734F6.title: "A Hotter Place"
	quest.48F829CC00DB284A.quest_desc: ["bury a lit campfire so no air reaches it, put logs on it, and wait. patience is the main ingredient. notice that too hot ruins the logs and a bellows lets air in, which is exactly what you do not want here."]
	quest.48F829CC00DB284A.title: "Charcoal Without Air"
	quest.4A10E1BFC1F0C7BC.quest_desc: ["make your first tool or part out of stone, wood or bone. the &6&lstone age&r covers wood, bone, stone, granite, diorite, andesite, basalt, deepslate, tuff and obsidian." "" "finding a tool lying around does not count. you get into an age by making something, in the crafting grid, at a part bench or at the engineering table."]
	quest.4A10E1BFC1F0C7BC.title: "Stone Age"
	quest.4A62ADC8F2D5DBAE.quest_desc: ["draws nearby orbs into your vessels, so you stop chasing glowing dots. pair it with an &6&lxp meter&r to read what you have."]
	quest.4A62ADC8F2D5DBAE.title: "Orb Absorber"
	quest.4A9F5BB8C3BA0D7E.quest_desc: ["nothing is rolled. an enchantment is an attunement written onto one part by tracing letters with a pen, so handwriting finally matters. edge, ward, yield and hold work at level 1 without a rite."]
	quest.4A9F5BB8C3BA0D7E.title: "Enchanting Table"
	quest.4ABFA74C87F277EC.quest_desc: ["an &6&lelectromagnet&r pulls dropped iron and steel toward it, and shoves diamagnetic material away. make one and watch what it picks up. it has strong opinions." "" "warning: it is built for lv. feeding it more only wears it down. it needs &d&o&nelectrical treatise ii&r."]
	quest.4ABFA74C87F277EC.title: "Iron Hunter"
	quest.4B3E8636338ECF59.quest_desc: ["current through a bath pulls metal out of solution. an &6&lelectrolytic cell&r can refine an alloy back to a pure metal or plate one metal onto another, a spa day for ingots." "" "hang the anode, fill the bath with water, acid or lye, and keep to lv. it needs both &d&o&nchemical treatise i&r and &d&o&nelectrical treatise i&r."]
	quest.4B3E8636338ECF59.title: "Plating and Refining"
	quest.4B40D895308340D8.quest_desc: ["Built from parts, not picked from a list."]
	quest.4B40D895308340D8.title: "Weapons"
	quest.4BC474359EF5F912.quest_desc: ["wash dirt, gravel or mud in water for clay, then fire it. &6&lbrick&rs are the stuff of nearly every furnace part, so get used to the sight of them."]
	quest.4BC474359EF5F912.title: "Clay and Brick"
	quest.4C37DC421C72969E.quest_desc: ["&d&o&nexperience treatise iii&r: spending it opens the &6&ldisenchanting stone&r. the stone does the unmaking, and you get the change back."]
	quest.4C37DC421C72969E.title: "Spend It"
	quest.4D0EA602FA913EBC.quest_desc: ["the &6&lelectric controller&r is a controller you program electrically and that talks to more of the world. it builds on a controller, a memory board and a circuit, so bring your whole résumé."]
	quest.4D0EA602FA913EBC.title: "Electric Brain"
	quest.4D1678088F6B0EE8.quest_desc: ["buy from a villager, or sell it something. capitalism, but small and green." "" "standing with the village sets the prices."]
	quest.4D1678088F6B0EE8.title: "Fair Trade"
	quest.4D18E2ED429337DB.quest_desc: ["an exosuit is ordinary modular armor with fittings added at the engineering table's fit tab: a servo (a finished dynamotor), a &6&lbattery&r bay in the chestplate, and a sensor head in the helmet. the battery powers strength, jump and dash, plating, night sight and thermal view." "" "without a battery or with it flat, the suit is dead weight, never a lock. a very expensive coat rack, but never a locked door."]
	quest.4D18E2ED429337DB.title: "Battery for the Suit"
	quest.4D67C70FD4A2C46F.quest_desc: ["get a &6&lgalvanic cell&r item in hand. notice that the anode wears away as it works, and that its shape trades current against lifetime. everything is a trade, even the chemistry."]
	quest.4D67C70FD4A2C46F.title: "Cell on the Bench"
	quest.4D9912C3F2925E59.quest_desc: ["&6&laerospace treatise ii: thrusters&r. opens thrusters. propellers were the warm-up act." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with aerospace i held and mechanical ii held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.4D9912C3F2925E59.title: "Aerospace Treatise II"
	quest.4DB13A508EF6750A.quest_desc: ["build a bed: a mattress on a frame, set down as a place you can respawn. fancy." "" "a frame adds comfort and warmth, and weight. nothing is free, not even a nap."]
	quest.4DB13A508EF6750A.title: "Off the Floor"
	quest.4E189D5AA01C6BC0.quest_desc: ["a cat's whisker touching a crystal passes current one way. seat a crystal, then right-click to step among spots on its face, and notice that some are dead and some are sharp. finding a good spot takes patience." "" "   &c&otoo much current burns a spot out.&r"]
	quest.4E189D5AA01C6BC0.title: "The Whisker"
	quest.4EE541AC01486CE2.quest_desc: ["a &6&ldifferential&r lets two outputs turn at different speeds and can be set to open, limited slip or locked. it is very good at being diplomatic."]
	quest.4EE541AC01486CE2.title: "Differential"
	quest.4F1E41836AC8629A.quest_desc: ["stand within reach of a hearth that is lit and holding heat." "" "the hearth keeps an anvil's stock warm, and keeps you warm too. it is a small domestic miracle."]
	quest.4F1E41836AC8629A.title: "Warm Room"
	quest.4F639FCBD0437179.quest_desc: ["the spark reader records the &6&lkind&r of the goods, one more band to sort on."]
	quest.4F639FCBD0437179.title: "Kind"
	quest.4F94A73D1AFCAA05.quest_desc: ["a &6&lgrinding wheel&r shapes the hardest stock, and its grit is consumed on every cut. work heats as it is ground, so it is a hungry and warm little machine."]
	quest.4F94A73D1AFCAA05.title: "Grinding Wheel"
	quest.4FC8262913B96623.quest_desc: ["bastion rubble and piglins killed by a player may drop bits. bastion chests may hold rubble. the piglins did not volunteer."]
	quest.4FC8262913B96623.title: "Worn Netherite Bits"
	quest.4FF83B65BCE51C84.quest_desc: ["slow a line down, speed it up, or send it around a corner. a &6&lsmall cog&r goes around a shaft and a &6&llarge cog&r goes around a &6&lsmall cog&r." "" "try meshing different sizes and see what happens to speed and force. loops of gears that disagree with each other will jam, and gears hold a grudge."]
	quest.4FF83B65BCE51C84.title: "Cogs and Corners"
	quest.501EBB7F716B3666.quest_desc: ["a node on the xp wire that harvests a ripe culture dish beside it, in the dark, for run xp. it holds none of its own, and the dish sets the pace."]
	quest.501EBB7F716B3666.title: "Sculk Grower"
	quest.50CCAA2AA559EC7C.quest_desc: ["copper melts in a fire you can build. find a vessel that holds the melt, set it over a firebox, and put copper in." "" "warning: a cold &6&lpour&r into a brick or glass pot can crack it, so warm the pot first. if the tank is full, extra melt is lost, and it does not apologize."]
	quest.50CCAA2AA559EC7C.title: "Pour"
	quest.50CDE297CFB5626D.quest_desc: ["a board of sixteen job slots that a fleet of robots shares over radio. robots with a radio part in range can claim a slot, finish it or post a job, and a claim lapses if the robot goes quiet. it only hears as many robots as its power allows. needs &d&o&nrobotics treatise ii&r: robots." "" "a crowded fleet also steps more slowly. a very small office, with a very small queue."]
	quest.50CDE297CFB5626D.title: "Robot Job Board"
	quest.5131B0901ECB69D3.quest_desc: ["what the nether gives is not yet usable. melt it down and cast it. raw debris is a rough draft."]
	quest.5131B0901ECB69D3.title: "Debris, Refined"
	quest.5167E7B516876AA7.quest_desc: ["an &6&loscilloscope&r draws a waveform on a &6&lphosphor screen&r, and it is surprisingly pretty. make the screen by sealing glass on a firebox. reheating or a splash of water shatters it."]
	quest.5167E7B516876AA7.title: "See the Signal"
	quest.51D26155DF410D5C.quest_desc: ["a &6&lrectifier&r lets current go one way and sits touching a battery. it needs a crystal detector to be of any use; see the control chapter. a bouncer for electrons."]
	quest.51D26155DF410D5C.title: "One-Way Street"
	quest.5212324AD4B931AA.quest_desc: ["plain glass softens early. pure silica holds its shape much hotter, and wants a much hotter fire. fancy glass has fancy demands."]
	quest.5212324AD4B931AA.title: "Clearer Still"
	quest.521249D2A2E00425.quest_desc: ["mined as in vanilla. it will not smelt to scrap here, and no smithing upgrade exists. it melts. the old shortcut is closed for renovations."]
	quest.521249D2A2E00425.title: "Ancient Debris"
	quest.521F4FBCFD71471D.quest_desc: ["&c&ochaos points come from causing a new kind of disorder on a target: burning, bleeding, blinding, tripping, stripping armor.&r each kind pays once per target. repeats pay less, and training dummies stop paying. mischief has diminishing returns, sadly." "" "make a note once you hold some points in the chaos tree."]
	quest.521F4FBCFD71471D.quest_subtitle: "Earn your first points."
	quest.521F4FBCFD71471D.title: "Chaos: Earn Points"
	quest.53D735D818749101.quest_desc: ["&6&lchemical treatise ii: heat and compression&r opens the gas &6&lcompressor&r. it moves gas only, and compressing heats the gas, because physics likes to bill you twice. naphtha vapor is the one to watch."]
	quest.53D735D818749101.title: "Squeeze"
	quest.53F81065C2898257.quest_desc: ["a &6&lrotary bearing&r turns whatever you build in front of it. right-click with an empty hand to bring the built piece to life, and again to put it back, like a tiny frankenstein switch." "" "sneak-use cycles its role: turn with the shaft, steer, or work as a roll, pitch or yaw surface."]
	quest.53F81065C2898257.title: "Rotary Bearing"
	quest.53FCF31BE2083FFE.quest_desc: ["eat food that was &6&lkept cold&r and is still sound. a small victory, served chilled."]
	quest.53FCF31BE2083FFE.title: "Kept Cold"
	quest.5425EA12527503A4.quest_desc: ["a &d&o&ntreatise&r is a numbered book on one school of engineering. you keep it forever, and every volume is its own subject: holding ii does not magically hand you i. craft a &6&lblank treatise&r from two paper, leather and an ink sac, shapeless. yes, it is a diary for machines."]
	quest.5425EA12527503A4.title: "Blank Treatise"
	quest.54D88CEEE882B369.quest_desc: ["three of one material in a row make &6&lxp wire&r: paper, quartz, amethyst and others carry it differently. some of them are better at it than others, and paper has noticeably tried."]
	quest.54D88CEEE882B369.title: "XP Wire"
	quest.54ECA7CE07A3BA48.quest_desc: ["reflexes are fixed. build something you can tell what to do, then give it something to read." "" "the mechanical controller runs on a turning shaft and reads programs from punch cards. it is a switch, not a dial. it needs &d&o&nmechanical treatise ii&r."]
	quest.54ECA7CE07A3BA48.title: "A Thermostat"
	quest.558657879EC52D94.quest_desc: ["make your first tool or part out of wrought or cast iron. the prologue ends here and the sciences open up: electricity, heat and blaze, xp and sculk." "" "notice that iron is the first metal a plain fire cannot work. it has opinions about your campfire."]
	quest.558657879EC52D94.title: "Iron Age"
	quest.563AB428B0FFAA56.quest_desc: ["a &6&lconveyor belt&r carries things at the speed of the shaft behind its head. modules on top of it sort, weigh, cool and count what rides. it is basically a tiny airport."]
	quest.563AB428B0FFAA56.title: "Belt Line"
	quest.56650DFDC3221BB5.quest_desc: ["&6&lelectrical treatise i: cells and static charge&r. opens batteries, galvanic cells, leyden jars, generators and several instruments. you start out gently, with a small spark and a smaller ego." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.56650DFDC3221BB5.title: "Electrical Treatise I"
	quest.575A3F9848B9C704.quest_desc: ["rivers stay put. make a shaft turn on fire, anywhere, which sounds worse than it is." "" "place a steam engine touching the boiler. one engine is not very strong: it will not run a hammer alone, so do not ask it to."]
	quest.575A3F9848B9C704.title: "Fire on a Shaft"
	quest.57F7848FDFE7469F.quest_desc: ["&6&lmechanical treatise ii: transmission&r. opens transmissions, gearboxes, differentials, the pivot mast, controllers and the derrick base. for when one spinning thing is not enough and you want it to be somebody else's problem too." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with mechanical i held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.57F7848FDFE7469F.title: "Mechanical Treatise II"
	quest.587ADD74E5A9E31D.quest_desc: ["some fires need no fuel and have no gap. &c&oset a vessel where one burns.&r lava holds a vessel just under a fixed &b1200 tu&r, too cool for steel." "" "&c&owarning: lava burns.&r you will regret finding that out the hard way."]
	quest.587ADD74E5A9E31D.title: "Fire That Does Not Go Out"
	quest.58D2BB7C92A33393.quest_desc: ["nitrogen can be pulled from air over a charcoal sieve bed, and combined with hydrogen over a bed of iron. notice the temperature windows. they are picky, and they will not be talked round."]
	quest.58D2BB7C92A33393.title: "Ammonia"
	quest.5921987543C125B2.quest_desc: ["a &6&lgas centrifuge&r splits uranium into enriched and depleted fractions. notice that the rotor can tear itself apart if spun too fast. patience is cheaper than a new rotor."]
	quest.5921987543C125B2.title: "Enrichment"
	quest.5B32C0F8AADE715C.quest_desc: ["a powder that pushes a growing crop on like bone meal. notice that it scorches one that is already grown: harvest first. it comes from the chemistry side, and it has opinions about timing."]
	quest.5B32C0F8AADE715C.title: "Fertiliser"
	quest.5B3DF54E8F8E2F79.quest_desc: ["a telescope is an &6&lobjective lens&r, an &6&leyepiece lens&r and a &6&ltelescope tube&r. the tube length matters, since it follows the focal lengths. measure twice, grumble once."]
	quest.5B3DF54E8F8E2F79.title: "Grind a Lens"
	quest.5BBAB64A70CA5A5C.quest_desc: ["a &6&lbullet mold&r, a ball mold or a hammered nugget makes bullets. shape matters: round nose, round ball, flat nose, pointed, hollow point. the bullet has a fashion sense."]
	quest.5BBAB64A70CA5A5C.title: "Cast a Bullet"
	quest.5C0679CA97A25064.quest_desc: ["a &6&lcurrent sensor&r bolts to a cable face and lets a controller watch how much current passes, a nosy neighbor with a purpose. it needs &d&o&nelectrical treatise iii&r."]
	quest.5C0679CA97A25064.title: "Read the Line"
	quest.5C130D124152051E.quest_desc: ["&d&o&nexperience treatise ii&r: &6&ltaps&r opens the &6&lore tap&r, &6&ltrade tap&r and &6&lsmelter tap&r. with no trade tap in reach a counter pays no xp at all. no tap, no tip."]
	quest.5C130D124152051E.title: "Taps"
	quest.5C526BFB2E217475.quest_desc: ["a drum on a shaft beats wheat apart into seed, &6&lstraw&r and chaff. it needs a spinning shaft and the first &d&o&nmechanical treatise&r. anything harder than its teeth jams it, so do not feed it your feelings."]
	quest.5C526BFB2E217475.title: "Threshing"
	quest.5C8D7712CBB15731.quest_desc: ["a rarer basin lies under the deep dark, marked by &6&lecho seep&rs on cave floors. the survey meter reads it as an &6&lecho crude&r basin. the oil carries experience, and a fractionating column concentrates it in the heavy bottoms. &c&oa wellhead lifting it rings, then shrieks, then bursts if it is run too fast; flywheel inertia on the shaft damps it.&r"]
	quest.5C8D7712CBB15731.title: "Echo Crude"
	quest.5D34168FC4ADB432.quest_desc: ["hand-made parts are loose and rough, a bit like a first pancake. make a machine cut to size." "" "the lathe turns rod, cuts coil springs and makes screws and machine bolts. be aware it needs fasteners itself, so hand-file a few to start, and yes, the irony is noted. cutting a first part on a lathe, drill press or grinding wheel is how you enter the machine age."]
	quest.5D34168FC4ADB432.title: "Tolerances"
	quest.5D981E09BACA3BA9.quest_desc: ["deliver work a villager calls exceptional." "" "a villager names the one thing furthest off. use that, and try to look like you meant it."]
	quest.5D981E09BACA3BA9.title: "Master's Mark"
	quest.5DAA24750E10BDF3.quest_desc: ["heavy oil can be cracked over a catalyst bed in the reactor into diesel and naphtha. past the upper temperature the bed cokes, so watch your temperature readings. &c&oa burnt bed is a sad bed.&r"]
	quest.5DAA24750E10BDF3.title: "Crack It"
	quest.5DAE8F639F0F0E30.quest_desc: ["&6&laerospace treatise i: propellers&r. opens propellers. the humble start of leaving the ground on purpose." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.5DAE8F639F0F0E30.title: "Aerospace Treatise I"
	quest.5E1C8B0A762D4685.quest_desc: ["cast a &6&ltechnique&r from any skill tree. slot it, then fire it with its cast key or the radial. casts cost stamina and rearm on a timer, a landed blow, a stagger or a parry. not free, but cheaper than regret."]
	quest.5E1C8B0A762D4685.title: "Technique"
	quest.5E42A189D61F4A55.quest_desc: ["cooking is hand work too. find a table to prepare things on." "" "the &6&lprep table&r takes a hand knife where a forging bench takes a hammer, and it is where containers and dishes are made. it is a forge for people who like lunch."]
	quest.5E42A189D61F4A55.title: "Prep Work"
	quest.5F2E6F38D730DC4A.quest_desc: ["break a block that needs the right tool, with a hafted tool that is one." "" "notice that the right head on the right block is the whole point. a spoon is still a bad shovel."]
	quest.5F2E6F38D730DC4A.title: "Fit for Purpose"
	quest.5F32E556521D4BD8.quest_desc: ["a &6&lglove&r body of leather, plus a metacarpal plate, makes a &6&lfighting glove&r. a bare hand in one can parry blows, though not projectiles. arrows are still, regrettably, faster than a glove."]
	quest.5F32E556521D4BD8.title: "Fighting Glove"
	quest.5FAAA83895291728.quest_desc: ["&c&oenriched fuel burns hotter.&r make an &6&lenriched fuel rod&r, and then treat it with a bit more respect."]
	quest.5FAAA83895291728.title: "Enriched Fuel"
	quest.5FD512D276B299FE.quest_desc: ["a &6&lcharger&r clips onto a battery item and fills it from a line. make one, then give some thought to what powered armor or tools might use it."]
	quest.5FD512D276B299FE.title: "Charge Up"
	quest.602A518B1C000E05.quest_desc: ["the belt slot piece: one plate and two leather. it holds up your dignity, more or less."]
	quest.602A518B1C000E05.title: "Sash"
	quest.6062E7D8E826525E.quest_desc: ["three bricks in a row. right-click a crucible with an empty mold to fill it. the most humble piece of equipment in the chapter."]
	quest.6062E7D8E826525E.title: "Ingot Mold"
	quest.618D82E9909540F5.quest_desc: ["containers decide which dish you get. make a bowl, a plate or a skewer from stock. the plate is doing a lot of the work here."]
	quest.618D82E9909540F5.title: "Bowls and Skewers"
	quest.61E193D19E789F30.quest_desc: ["watch a creature take aim at you, and be somewhere else when it lets go. skeletons telegraph; the bow draw is the tell. frankly it is polite of them."]
	quest.61E193D19E789F30.title: "Read the Draw"
	quest.628D750EE641B7B5.quest_desc: ["distill the slurry in a fractionating column to unstable &6&lsolvent&r, then damp it in the reactor with lapis and a trace of heavy water." "" "warning: solvent vapor teleports things at random. that includes you, and it will not ask where you wanted to go."]
	quest.628D750EE641B7B5.title: "Solvent"
	quest.62BCFEF2B4988306.quest_desc: ["use a technique from the veil tree. be elsewhere. be convincingly elsewhere."]
	quest.62BCFEF2B4988306.title: "Unseen"
	quest.62F7CF7ED138776D.quest_desc: ["observation points come from landed blows with a precise weapon, and from placed hits: at the tip of reach, from range with a bow, or on a creature you have sized up. repeats pay less, and training dummies stop paying. they are not worth studying." "" "make a note once you hold some points in the observation tree. you were probably going to anyway."]
	quest.62F7CF7ED138776D.quest_subtitle: "Earn your first points."
	quest.62F7CF7ED138776D.title: "Observation: Earn Points"
	quest.634264D94C971FE2.quest_desc: ["terracotta and wool. set against crucible sides, each block cuts heat loss. it makes a crucible steadier, not hotter than the fire. a sweater for your pot, basically."]
	quest.634264D94C971FE2.title: "Insulation"
	quest.63589FDA8F8B4D36.quest_desc: ["a hook on a line you throw, then winch in, release with sneak, or pay out. fittings go in the grid with the parts: more line, a winch, a barbed head, a second hook. consider it a very ambitious fishing trip."]
	quest.63589FDA8F8B4D36.title: "Grapple"
	quest.637ACEE50B401F84.quest_desc: ["rub something and hear it snap. electricity begins as a tiny, useless-looking charge, and your first job is making it show up on purpose." "" "&d&o&nelectrical treatise i&r covers the cells and static machines in this chapter. each &d&o&ntreatise&r volume stands alone, so no homework from the previous one."]
	quest.637ACEE50B401F84.title: "Static Cling"
	quest.63D584E6C3A70AFF.quest_desc: ["both ends of a pair must be loaded. a &6&lchunk anchor&r keeps a port's chunk loaded, so the parcel does not arrive at a locked door."]
	quest.63D584E6C3A70AFF.title: "Chunk Anchor"
	quest.640493A814B77267.quest_desc: ["a &6&llocked joint&r holds a body rigid. with an empty hand and nothing in front of it but another body touching the cell, it docks that body. use it again to let go with a spring kick." "" "link one to a controller and it has a release channel: a card level of half or more lets go, so a rocket can drop a spent stage."]
	quest.640493A814B77267.title: "Letting Go"
	quest.6408CCDFD43EBA76.quest_desc: ["the heat has to go somewhere, and it will choose if you do not. a &6&lheat exchanger&r moves it toward a boiler and turbine."]
	quest.6408CCDFD43EBA76.title: "Carry the Heat Away"
	quest.646843916B048173.quest_desc: ["a &6&lsoldering iron&r joins a pasted board by hand: heat it at a fire, hold the board in the other hand, and drag along the pads. &c&oshiny joints are good, dull ones cold, dark ones burnt.&r" "" "&c&owarning: leaded solder poisons you while it is worked or molten.&r your hobby is technically a health hazard."]
	quest.646843916B048173.title: "Hot Iron"
	quest.64ACD780CE1D0648.quest_desc: ["a finished thing is named by what it is made of and how it is built, read off by rule. notice what your piece gets called. it may not be what you called it."]
	quest.64ACD780CE1D0648.title: "Designations"
	quest.6508144C4BE3DC6D.quest_desc: ["potions can be poured into a stockpot or onto a dish. fine palate and assay reveal what has been &6&llaced&r. trust, but verify, then trust a bit less."]
	quest.6508144C4BE3DC6D.title: "Laced"
	quest.653C83AE36A9E247.quest_desc: ["seat a round at the press: set the bore, add the case, charge and bullet, and press. it also makes shot shells, launcher shells and rockets. &d&o&nweapons treatise ii&r: firearms. a satisfying hobby for people who like small, loud things."]
	quest.653C83AE36A9E247.title: "Reloading Press"
	quest.6545178999CAF6DB.quest_desc: ["   &c&oa valve between boiler and engine gives you control, and also lets you trap a pressure that will hurt you.&r &c&oshutting steam off on a hot fire is how boilers burst, so this one comes with a handle and a warning.&r"]
	quest.6545178999CAF6DB.title: "Valve"
	quest.65604B388F658610.quest_desc: ["a pulse barrel and a seat that stores a charge, powered from a battery. &c&ono powder burns, but heat does build; heat governors cut off before it hurts.&r needs &d&o&nweapons treatise iii&r: &6&lelectric gun&rs." "" "&c&oshock is a real hazard.&r you will regret ignoring it."]
	quest.65604B388F658610.title: "Electric Gun"
	quest.656F1A18EA70BC7B.quest_desc: ["&6&lelectrical treatise ii: coils and magnets&r. opens heating coils, linear motors, electromagnets, relays, rectifiers and the data sensor. the magnets are mostly fine. mostly." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with electrical i held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.656F1A18EA70BC7B.title: "Electrical Treatise II"
	quest.66073F1666530F34.quest_desc: ["eating, trading and getting by. nothing here is locked; these are just the things the pack quietly notices you doing."]
	quest.66073F1666530F34.title: "Survival"
	quest.668F7D1EE6B7EC9F.quest_desc: ["a &6&lbearing&r is a shaft that turns easily, and it is an ingredient in most machines. quietly important, like the person who always brings the snacks." "" "friction costs power per turn. a long run of plain shafts without support costs double, so fit a bearing now and then. this is built at the engineering table and needs &d&o&nmechanical treatise i&r."]
	quest.668F7D1EE6B7EC9F.title: "Less Friction"
	quest.66B73035DDD8E8F8.quest_desc: ["   &c&obreathe air a hot toxic metal has fouled.&r" "" "&c&osome metals give off fume when worked hot.&r open air and a respirator are kinder than a closed shed, and your lungs agree."]
	quest.66B73035DDD8E8F8.title: "Cough"
	quest.66EF47A785FCFF05.quest_desc: ["fit a head to a handle and build a tool. the oldest trick there is." "" "the parts and how they are shaped decide what the tool does."]
	quest.66EF47A785FCFF05.title: "Handy"
	quest.6714029728CEF6F8.quest_desc: ["wheat and water, worked by hand. raw &6&ldough&r is barely food: bake it into a &6&lloaf&r, or knead it at the prep table and see how it turns out. a bit of a gamble, as bread goes."]
	quest.6714029728CEF6F8.title: "Dough"
	quest.674423AE8376FA62.quest_desc: ["hold something glowing, and pay nothing for it. smugness optional." "" "tongs, insulation or a glove rated for the heat. notice which of them you reached for."]
	quest.674423AE8376FA62.title: "Cool Hand"
	quest.674CA97ADA4E3234.quest_desc: ["get hit while wearing armor you built, and take less for it. armor is made from plate, and the plate is the piece. being hit on purpose is optional but educational."]
	quest.674CA97ADA4E3234.title: "Worth the Weight"
	quest.6766D515656752AF.quest_desc: ["flip food in the pan so it does not brown on one side only. symmetry is a kind of respect."]
	quest.6766D515656752AF.title: "Spatula"
	quest.676B1FCA974B29A3.quest_desc: ["two different metals and a wet gap give a steady push with nothing moving, which feels like cheating. make a galvanic cell." "" "&6&la cell&r is drawn at the blueprint table, so its parts depend on what metals you choose. a close metal pair gives lv, a wider pair more."]
	quest.676B1FCA974B29A3.title: "A Cell"
	quest.679F18CC9784ADED.quest_desc: ["a &6&lrespirator&r takes a face piece, a strap and a filter or an air cylinder. &c&oa filter cuts the poison from fumes; it does not make radiation go away.&r do not mistake it for a force field."]
	quest.679F18CC9784ADED.title: "Breathe Easy"
	quest.68B112D66AEC9F04.quest_desc: ["press k to open &6&lthe skill screen&r. there are seven trees, each with its own pool of points, and points and learned nodes survive death. death takes plenty, but not this." "" "nothing here gates making anything. a skill nudges a figure or opens a technique the body could always attempt badly, and frequently did."]
	quest.68B112D66AEC9F04.quest_subtitle: "Press K and look around."
	quest.68B112D66AEC9F04.title: "The Skill Screen"
	quest.68B9F3D4A1316E97.quest_desc: ["earn a village's highest regard." "" "standing is how the village's people gossip about you. it shows when you open a ledger board. yes, they talk."]
	quest.68B9F3D4A1316E97.title: "Well Regarded"
	quest.68C871680B024316.quest_desc: ["cut a part to size on a lathe, drill press or grinding wheel: the first thing made by a machine, to a measure. this age has no materials of its own. players standing nearby get it too, so enjoy the free ride." "" "   &c&oradiation and flight open here.&r"]
	quest.68C871680B024316.title: "Machine Age"
	quest.6904675BDE404643.quest_desc: ["hold or touch something too hot for bare skin, and take the hit." "" "&c&ohot things burn a bare hand by how hot they are.&r &c&opay attention to what hurts, how much, and what you were holding.&r the lesson is usually free, and also not."]
	quest.6904675BDE404643.title: "Burn Notice"
	quest.69138601C3C58F1E.quest_desc: ["build an &6&lelectrostatic generator&r. a click gives a short pulse at high voltage band but stores nothing, and it throws a spark you can hear nearby. very dramatic, very unhelpful."]
	quest.69138601C3C58F1E.title: "Turn the Handle"
	quest.6923AC8A7841D33B.quest_desc: ["keep going until you have spent a good handful of points in the brute tree. some branches are exclusive: choosing one closes its sibling, so read before you learn. brute force does not work on the menu."]
	quest.6923AC8A7841D33B.quest_subtitle: "Spend a fair number of points."
	quest.6923AC8A7841D33B.title: "Brute: Spend Points"
	quest.6929599BFFB00AFB.quest_desc: ["thaumaturge-dependent. brush it on a placed block so that block does not corrode in a chunk flooded with flux. a &6&lscrubbing bed&r protects them all, which is the lazy and sensible option."]
	quest.6929599BFFB00AFB.title: "Taint Glaze (Thaumaturge)"
	quest.696ADBB37997C4EE.quest_desc: ["drive two &6&lpiton&rs and run a grapple between them for a fixed climbable line. the mountain stays put, which is the whole point."]
	quest.696ADBB37997C4EE.title: "Piton"
	quest.69866D4867693C05.quest_desc: ["a &6&lclutch&r lets you break a shaft line with a right-click. it does not brake, so the far side coasts on, blissfully unaware." "" "a hand-made clutch needs a coil spring, which is easier to turn once you have a lathe."]
	quest.69866D4867693C05.title: "Stop That Line"
	quest.69F062D9A3486F4D.quest_desc: ["a &6&lredstone coherer&r starts open. a nearby spark welds it shut, and right-clicking taps it open again. sparks come from breakers, relays and the static generator." "" "try a cell, a coherer and an electromagnet on one line, then crank a generator within earshot. you will hear it work."]
	quest.69F062D9A3486F4D.title: "Hear the Spark"
	quest.6A444ABB2CD68E96.quest_desc: ["a &6&lhopper&r moves one item straight into the block it faces. a chain of hoppers is a longer conveyor, and a very patient one."]
	quest.6A444ABB2CD68E96.title: "Hop Along"
	quest.6AA47E0C6C42F0AF.quest_desc: ["stir a flask over the plant map until you land inside an effect. miss and you get a dud draught, but a residue mark hints which kind of compound you missed. the pot needs warmth; below a low temperature nothing comes out, however hard you stir."]
	quest.6AA47E0C6C42F0AF.title: "First Draught"
	quest.6AE1678E347D298F.quest_desc: ["other attunements need a rite, researched at the research table and shelved on a ring of chiseled bookshelves around the table. the shelves are load-bearing, in a magical sense."]
	quest.6AE1678E347D298F.title: "Rites"
	quest.6B9D7BEDF4F83E9D.quest_desc: ["a &6&lcrossbow&r is a modular build around a prod. drawing its blueprint needs &d&o&nweapons treatise ii&r: firearms. the prod is as unglamorous as it sounds."]
	quest.6B9D7BEDF4F83E9D.title: "A Bolt in the Dark"
	quest.6BB9FDABE2C0C8EB.quest_desc: ["&d&o&nelectrical treatise i&r covers batteries, cells and static machines. a &d&o&ntreatise&r is kept, never consumed, so you can stop hoarding it nervously."]
	quest.6BB9FDABE2C0C8EB.title: "Treatise: Cells and Static Charge"
	quest.6BEA8E2C245BD75A.quest_desc: ["&6&lrobotics treatise i: suit modules&r. opens suit modules and the armor fittings of the exosuit. dressing up, but with engineering." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with mechanical i and electrical ii held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.6BEA8E2C245BD75A.title: "Robotics Treatise I"
	quest.6C59433EECF6DB4E.quest_desc: ["four xp containers seated as one node on the run, standing at their common level. a fuller vial gives to an emptier one. attuned machines draw their upkeep from the bank, and from a holder or wire touching them, rather than from whoever is nearby; below a minimum run level an attunement just goes quiet, and nothing is lost."]
	quest.6C59433EECF6DB4E.title: "Crystal Bank"
	quest.6C6DCC82A2C3A0F0.quest_desc: ["Armor, packs, suits, robots and the tables that build them."]
	quest.6C6DCC82A2C3A0F0.title: "Gear"
	quest.6C7D15FE7D905AD0.quest_desc: ["carry a counter or dosimeter through a dose sick enough to make you hungry, and come out the other side. a character-building stroll." "" "warning: dose is kept between sessions. carried sources count in full, and nearby blocks count less with distance. logging off is not a rinse cycle."]
	quest.6C7D15FE7D905AD0.title: "Counted Down"
	quest.6CAB0D61B3E339EC.quest_desc: ["have a villager buy from a counter you keep." "" "a villager needs a path to the front of the counter, and something it wants on the shelf. a sign saying \"open\" is not in the requirements."]
	quest.6CAB0D61B3E339EC.title: "Open for Business"
	quest.6CEB83D33A911A22.quest_desc: ["a &6&lcomponent tester&r reads whiskers, coherers, relays, boards and circuits. optional, but useful before you hand-solder a dozen boards and find out the hard way."]
	quest.6CEB83D33A911A22.title: "Check Your Work"
	quest.6D1A98D35E19FC80.quest_desc: ["experience can be held, if you find something to hold it. make an xp container, and stop leaving your levels lying around."]
	quest.6D1A98D35E19FC80.title: "Experience, Bottled"
	quest.6D73FE070DADDF0B.quest_desc: ["a shop &6&lcounter&r with a nine-slot shelf. stock it and villagers walk over and buy at your prices. you are now a shopkeeper, apologies."]
	quest.6D73FE070DADDF0B.title: "Counter"
	quest.6EB3711E876C19F1.quest_desc: ["make your first tool or part out of steel, tempered steel, hardened steel or manganese steel, with the carbon under control. chemistry and ender open from here." "" "steel wants more heat than a fuel fire gives up easily, and some care while it cools. it is a bit precious like that."]
	quest.6EB3711E876C19F1.title: "Steel Age"
	quest.6EEACE8D4A2185F6.quest_desc: ["&6&lexperience treatise iii: spending it&r. opens the disenchanting stone and converter tap. saving is nice, but the shop is open." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with experience ii held and electrical iii held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.6EEACE8D4A2185F6.title: "Experience Treatise III"
	quest.6F38AC1A6BB646C4.quest_desc: ["build a &6&lgeiger counter&r. it reads the rate before armor, and rates under a faint threshold are unreadable, so silence is not a promise."]
	quest.6F38AC1A6BB646C4.title: "Geiger Counter"
	quest.6FA5F1811246D70E.quest_desc: ["a &6&lbulk hopper fitting&r lets a bay hold one loose stuff by weight alone: grain, dust, crushed ore, swarf. no count limit, only mass. an item with a state of its own, like heat or wear, will not pour into it."]
	quest.6FA5F1811246D70E.title: "Loose Goods"
	quest.7007D12279978168.quest_desc: ["the deep dark answers to vibration. set something to hear it, and keep what it heard. eavesdropping, but on a cave."]
	quest.7007D12279978168.title: "Listening"
	quest.701182B34E61A2B0.quest_desc: ["open the proficiency tree and learn a node. field dressing is the root. later nodes need their prerequisites first, in the sensible order, like a good first aid kit."]
	quest.701182B34E61A2B0.quest_subtitle: "Learn your first node."
	quest.701182B34E61A2B0.title: "Proficiency: First Node"
	quest.701AD4797E2034DD.quest_desc: ["the second mechanical volume is about transmission: gearboxes, differentials, controllers and freewheels. the sequel is denser, as sequels tend to be."]
	quest.701AD4797E2034DD.title: "Mechanical Treatise II"
	quest.7083ACA00499FF96.quest_desc: ["put a part on a trace board, paste it, and solder it. failed joints lift the traces and ruin the board, and you will feel that one. a component tester will tell you what you have." "" "notice that the cheapest path goes through a printed board and a coherer."]
	quest.7083ACA00499FF96.title: "A Circuit"
	quest.708A00651AA77B3C.quest_desc: ["a dense gray ore melts at a fire you can already build. &c&oit is soft, and poison to handle carelessly.&r" "" "&c&owarning: lead is a poison.&r handle it with care, and no, the pun was not on purpose."]
	quest.708A00651AA77B3C.title: "Heavy Metal"
	quest.70B03227BAC523B7.quest_desc: ["Bearings, lifts, wheels, wings and the sky"]
	quest.70B03227BAC523B7.title: "Vehicles and Flight"
	quest.70D479159B7F9337.quest_desc: ["an engine on a stand goes nowhere. sit on something that does." "" "the seat drives nothing alone. it needs a controller to carry what you do to the machine, since a chair has opinions but no influence."]
	quest.70D479159B7F9337.title: "Driver's Seat"
	quest.71C236855B06CB65.quest_desc: ["open the anchor tree and learn a node. wider window is the root: it lengthens your parry window. later nodes need their prerequisites first, so no skipping to the fun part."]
	quest.71C236855B06CB65.quest_subtitle: "Learn your first node."
	quest.71C236855B06CB65.title: "Anchor: First Node"
	quest.71F23EC0CC6438C8.quest_desc: ["beat the slag out of a hot bloom at an anvil: light and heavy blows, turn it, and finish. heavy blows split the piece, and each reheat loses iron as scale. a hearth keeps it warm. it is a lot of hitting with a lot of rules."]
	quest.71F23EC0CC6438C8.title: "Wrought Iron"
	quest.7214DAC1E7B2AD0B.quest_desc: ["a spring or steam &6&llauncher&r throws shells and rockets. the fuse decides when they go off: a wick, a striker, impact or proximity. needs &d&o&nweapons treatise ii&r: firearms." "" "&c&oexplosives hurt whoever stands next to them.&r that includes you, and you were standing next to you."]
	quest.7214DAC1E7B2AD0B.title: "Launcher"
	quest.7233379C8E9CF69C.quest_desc: ["&c&oproficiency points are for deliberate acts: aiding an ally, handling a fume or radiation dose with protection, eating a well-cooked meal.&r taking a blow pays nothing. repeats pay less, and training dummies stop paying. pain is not a skill, whatever it feels like." "" "make a note once you hold some points in the proficiency tree."]
	quest.7233379C8E9CF69C.quest_subtitle: "Earn your first points."
	quest.7233379C8E9CF69C.title: "Proficiency: Earn Points"
	quest.723B8B2957D61257.quest_desc: ["use a technique from the brute tree. put your weight in it; subtlety was never on the menu."]
	quest.723B8B2957D61257.title: "Heavy Hand"
	quest.729290842F82D66C.quest_desc: ["heavy water is the bottleneck. it comes from enriched water in the electrolyser, around one part in twenty. plan your stock before your teleportant, unless you enjoy waiting."]
	quest.729290842F82D66C.title: "The Scarce Input"
	quest.72A02123C4D22D57.quest_desc: ["a &6&lprogrammer&r writes a program onto a blank &6&lpunch card&r. make one, and a card to try it on. yes, you are punching holes into cardboard for science."]
	quest.72A02123C4D22D57.title: "Punch It In"
	quest.73CA41E8EF3BB000.quest_desc: ["feedback has no list of guns. a gun is a receiver, barrel, action, trigger group and grip, with optional stock, sights and fittings, assembled at the engineering table holding &d&o&nweapons treatise ii&r: firearms. it is a lot of parts, and every one of them has opinions." "" "machine tools make better parts: a drill press for barrels, a lathe for grips, a grinding wheel for slides. the tool has to be harder than the metal."]
	quest.73CA41E8EF3BB000.title: "A Real Gun"
	quest.741BB3D272806B1D.quest_desc: ["take back goods a raider carried off." "" "raiders head for stocked counters and drop the goods where they die. guard your shelves, they have already clocked them."]
	quest.741BB3D272806B1D.title: "Recovered Goods"
	quest.741DF93743CE7BE8.quest_desc: ["a &6&lrotation adapter&r joins full-size rotation to the finespace world. a translator for things that spin at different scales."]
	quest.741DF93743CE7BE8.title: "Fine Print"
	quest.743A3769BCA84A04.quest_desc: ["drive current through water or brine and see what comes apart. the electrolyser needs both &d&o&nchemical treatise i&r and &d&o&nelectrical treatise i&r, and medium voltage. hydrogen collects at the back, oxygen at the front." "" "warning: keep the electrode tanks drained. &c&ochlorine in a full tank poisons the area, and it is not shy about it.&r"]
	quest.743A3769BCA84A04.title: "Hydrogen on Tap"
	quest.747F1C88B4BBEABE.quest_desc: ["fuel sits in channels in a lattice, with graphite between to slow the neutrons and control assemblies to take them up. make a &6&lfuel channel&r, a &6&lgraphite moderator&r and a control assembly. it is a very crowded lattice."]
	quest.747F1C88B4BBEABE.title: "Channels and Moderators"
	quest.74B63C358E819FA4.quest_desc: ["run a wire to a machine no shaft can reach. freedom, finally." "" "cable comes in gauges, from thin to bus bar. &c&onotice that a cable asked for more current than it can carry heats up, burns off its insulation, and eventually fails.&r &c&obare live cable shocks you, and armor does not help, so do not get brave.&r"]
	quest.74B63C358E819FA4.title: "Work, Anywhere"
	quest.74E2CB341CE4E1E4.quest_desc: ["a &6&lcartridge&r is a drawn metal case, a charge and a bullet. learn what each part does: the case holds the pressure, the charge sets the push, the bullet carries it." "" "overpressure damages a gun, and a hot gun can cook a round off on its own. that is called a bad day."]
	quest.74E2CB341CE4E1E4.title: "Rounds Downrange"
	quest.750A788C860C063C.quest_desc: ["make a &6&lmemory drum&r and a &6&lmemory board&r. they hold program and data beyond what cards alone can, for when the cardboard pile gets embarrassing."]
	quest.750A788C860C063C.title: "Boards and Drums"
	quest.7523352D731BEC90.quest_desc: ["&b500 mb&r of hydrochloric acid in a thermal vessel dissolves a spent fuel rod into &6&lplutonium&r nuggets. &c&oplutonium is a metal with no ore, only ingots, and it is toxic as well as radioactive.&r" "" "an engineering table turns plutonium ingots and stainless plates into the strongest fuel rod there is. handle with every precaution you own."]
	quest.7523352D731BEC90.title: "Plutonium"
	quest.7534CF0E7D49FB41.quest_desc: ["bricks and an iron ingot, set on top of a firebox. it settles a little below the fire's heat and keeps stock in an anvil hot. &c&oa hot hearth burns bare hands, so do not get comfortable.&r"]
	quest.7534CF0E7D49FB41.title: "Hearth"
	quest.75BDB140C906FEB7.quest_desc: ["a beacon a robot can navigate toward. a lighthouse for the very small."]
	quest.75BDB140C906FEB7.title: "Robot Beacon"
	quest.75C360542D507892.quest_desc: ["a fuel fire tops out and makes smoke. find a heat that does not. you will have to leave the comfort of your firebox."]
	quest.75C360542D507892.title: "Hotter than Fire"
	quest.75F093FE062CF6EE.quest_desc: ["steam cracking naphtha gives ethylene, and ethylene under pressure with a catalyst becomes polyethylene melt. polyester and ptfe are longer branches, for when you want a hobby."]
	quest.75F093FE062CF6EE.title: "Polymers"
	quest.76765F09BC05E3C5.quest_desc: ["the &6&lcryocooler&r liquefies air in stages, and colder stages separate nitrogen, argon and helium. needs &d&o&nchemical treatise ii&r. helium is the safe lift gas, the one that will not set anything on fire."]
	quest.76765F09BC05E3C5.title: "Cold Snap"
	quest.7683F232CBDE1400.quest_desc: ["copper takes a second metal and turns the color of gold. not tin this time. about two parts copper to one of zinc. alchemists would be thrilled, and slightly offended."]
	quest.7683F232CBDE1400.title: "Yellow Metal"
	quest.7694E81268F128DA.quest_desc: ["hold &6&la dynamotor&r and think about which winding suits the engine on the other end of the shaft. slow engines want coarse windings; fast turbines want dense ones. match them like you would shoes."]
	quest.7694E81268F128DA.title: "A Dynamotor"
	quest.77CDEAF642129AE8.quest_desc: ["&6&lelectrical treatise iii: circuits&r. opens vacuum tubes, resonators, lattices, computers and the feedbacker. this is where the wires start to think they are clever." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with electrical ii held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.77CDEAF642129AE8.title: "Electrical Treatise III"
	quest.77DDFED06211ECE2.quest_desc: ["dissolve salt in water in the reactor, then split the brine in the electrolyser. &c&onotice what comes out: hydrogen, toxic chlorine, and lye that stays in the cell.&r one pot, three outcomes, only one of them friendly. water a pump draws from an ocean or beach pool already carries salt, does not mix with fresh water in a tank, and a vessel boiling it leaves salt behind."]
	quest.77DDFED06211ECE2.title: "Brine and Lye"
	quest.78418E720DEDA4BB.quest_desc: ["two bronze plates over four planks. it shapes metal parts with a hammer in the hammer slot. iron and steel must arrive hot; copper and bronze are worked cold."]
	quest.78418E720DEDA4BB.title: "Smithing Table"
	quest.7879AC3D4378E015.quest_desc: ["the &6&lsurvey meter&r reads whether you stand over an oil basin, which beats digging holes at random. a &6&lcopper bucket&r will scoop weathered crude from a tar seep: a small taste, never the basin drawn down."]
	quest.7879AC3D4378E015.title: "Read the Ground"
	quest.788E1A7BF5A5DCE5.quest_desc: ["a &6&lscram trip&r, with a bimetallic strip, drops all rods when the core gets too hot. build it into the shell. think of it as the emergency brake you hope to never admire."]
	quest.788E1A7BF5A5DCE5.title: "Scram Trip"
	quest.78DDBFB84F6C8568.quest_desc: ["each essentia crystal is a brewing stand ingredient too. on the alchemy map it walks toward the node of its own effect."]
	quest.78DDBFB84F6C8568.title: "Crystals in the Pot (Thaumaturge)"
	quest.793388EC7C1F0A58.quest_desc: ["the frozen moon has &6&lnitrogen ice&r in its ground. warm it to about minus &b205 tu&r and it melts into nitrogen. the crystal world is rich in amethyst geodes."]
	quest.793388EC7C1F0A58.title: "Planet Prizes"
	quest.79419957CE54EF03.quest_desc: ["&c&ochemical treatise iii: explosives.&r opens the demolition charge. it is the short chapter, and the loudest one." "" "ways to get it: write it from a specimen, research it at the research table for 40 xp with chemical ii held, find it in chests, or buy it from a villager at a high trade level."]
	quest.79419957CE54EF03.title: "Chemical Treatise III"
	quest.79938B1C86A26278.quest_desc: ["a &6&llathe bit&r, a &6&ldrill bit&r and an &6&labrasive wheel&r are the cutting edges of the other machines. they do the real work while the big machines take the credit."]
	quest.79938B1C86A26278.title: "Bits and Wheels"
	quest.799FECDFA99514BB.quest_desc: ["get a crop seed. crops grow by the weather: slower out of their comfortable band, halted below frost, never killed. they sulk, but they do not give up."]
	quest.799FECDFA99514BB.title: "Seeds"
	quest.79A867F222520386.quest_desc: ["keep going until you have spent a good handful of points in the onslaught tree. some branches are exclusive: choosing one closes its sibling, so read before you learn. yes, even if you are in a hurry."]
	quest.79A867F222520386.quest_subtitle: "Spend a fair number of points."
	quest.79A867F222520386.title: "Onslaught: Spend Points"
	quest.79BDA124A0641476.quest_desc: ["farmers, butchers, fishermen and shepherds order dishes. make one and deliver it. the customer is always hungry."]
	quest.79BDA124A0641476.title: "A Dish for an Order"
	quest.79FDC13FE72AC335.quest_desc: ["netherite melts at &b2600 tu&r, hotter than any fuel fire. notice that the hearth wears at high heat; a lining helps. even bricks get tired."]
	quest.79FDC13FE72AC335.title: "Hotter Still"
	quest.7A18478403772572.quest_desc: ["everything starts with stone, wood and no fire you actually control. six ages track how far your materials have come, and this chapter is the spine holding them together."]
	quest.7A18478403772572.title: "Technology"
	quest.7A251582C448924A.quest_desc: ["a thruster carries all it throws. a jet borrows the rest from the sky, which is thrifty." "" "needs &d&o&naerospace treatise iii&r. it cannot light itself from standstill: it wants a turning shaft or fast air. slamming the throttle stalls it, so be gentle with the lever."]
	quest.7A251582C448924A.title: "Breathing Fire"
	quest.7B3B6E5D6ECA8432.quest_desc: ["fuel is wood and coal. the ground has more, and has been quietly sitting on it. oil basins hide in the overworld underground, and tar seeps mark them. place a wellhead to claim some."]
	quest.7B3B6E5D6ECA8432.title: "Black Gold"
	quest.7B40851AEADBF414.quest_desc: ["exhaust steam vents to the air and is lost, which is a bit sad. a &6&lcondenser&r turns it back into water so a pump can feed the boiler again." "" "it only works below boiling, so the heat has to go somewhere. think about how you cool it, because the condenser certainly is."]
	quest.7B40851AEADBF414.title: "Close the Loop"
	quest.7B4C23CED4A90337.quest_desc: ["a spear sweeps a long, thin box in front of you instead of a single point, which is geometry nobody asked for and everybody benefits from. hold the use key while you land a hit and notice how it differs from just swinging."]
	quest.7B4C23CED4A90337.quest_subtitle: "Land a hit with a spear while the use key is held."
	quest.7B4C23CED4A90337.title: "Point Taken"
	quest.7B5346F28EFB8F55.quest_desc: ["soul oil seeps in the nether, or can be retorted from soul sand in the reactor. &c&oit burns hot and brings its own oxygen, so it does not need your permission to burn.&r"]
	quest.7B5346F28EFB8F55.title: "Soul Cooking"
	quest.7B83BC138D2C2F7A.quest_desc: ["&c&oa tank, a nozzle, a receiver and a valve throw water, hot fluid or burning fluid.&r under a minimum pressure nothing leaves the nozzle. needs &d&o&nweapons treatise ii&r." "" "&c&oburning fluid and hot fluid scald the caster as readily as the target.&r it is not picky about who it is angry at."]
	quest.7B83BC138D2C2F7A.title: "Fluid Caster"
	quest.7C053E54FFEF4495.quest_desc: ["a &6&lcontroller&r reads cards and signals and tells machines what to do. &d&o&nmechanical treatise ii&r covers it. finally, something in this pack that takes orders."]
	quest.7C053E54FFEF4495.title: "Controller"
	quest.7D0106CA2B287909.quest_desc: ["several cells wired in series push harder, like a very patient choir. pack them and notice how many it takes to climb a band."]
	quest.7D0106CA2B287909.title: "Cells in Series"
	quest.7DC88691608DD963.quest_desc: ["a shell and a strap make a pack for the curios back slot. open it with b. the strap's strength sets how much you can carry before you slow down. overload and it will cost you speed and sprinting. every hoarder meets this wall eventually."]
	quest.7DC88691608DD963.title: "Backpack"
	quest.7DDD38791AA20037.quest_desc: ["the &6&lbrewing stand&r replaces the vanilla one, and it has ambitions. make a &6&lmortar&r and a stand, and set a pot of water over a fire."]
	quest.7DDD38791AA20037.title: "Mortar and Pot"
	quest.7DEAA4FFB7092ADA.quest_desc: ["grinding a brick on a wheel gives a substrate. add redstone dust to print traces, or fine wire to etch ones that can carry power, and you have a &6&ltrace board&r. a brick, but make it fancy."]
	quest.7DEAA4FFB7092ADA.title: "A Flat Board"
	quest.7DF81153094E66D8.quest_desc: ["a &6&lfreewheel&r is an overrunning clutch: one side may spin faster than the side that drives it. a rare case of the passenger overtaking the driver."]
	quest.7DF81153094E66D8.title: "Freewheel"
	quest.7E1345D57EA0162A.quest_desc: ["&6&laerospace treatise iv: the wandering lights&r. it opens no types; it is a record of what you saw in the sky. all that staring up finally gets you a souvenir." "" "comes with your first resolved telescope sighting of a planet, together with a sky notebook."]
	quest.7E1345D57EA0162A.title: "Aerospace Treatise IV"
	quest.7E635D5E86C39D54.quest_desc: ["Machines that cut, press and draw metal"]
	quest.7E635D5E86C39D54.title: "Machine Shop"
	quest.7ED51153DEFF9BC9.quest_desc: ["&c&oa fuse holder takes a length of fine wire that carries current up to a point and then burns through.&r choose the metal so the fuse blows before the cable does. be the cheap thing that dies first."]
	quest.7ED51153DEFF9BC9.title: "Something Cheaper to Lose"
	quest.7FC1402563E5D2BC.quest_desc: ["a &6&lflux meter&r reads a core when you right-click it. use it to know what is going on in there, instead of guessing and hoping."]
	quest.7FC1402563E5D2BC.title: "Flux Meter"
}
